geosparql:asWKT rdfs:comment """
      The WKT serialization of a geometry
    """@en,
    "Well Known Text line string representing the geographical shape of the track"@en,
    "Well Known Text polygonal shape"@en .

<http://data.europa.eu/949/> rdfs:comment """This is the human and machine-readable Ontology governed by the European Union Agency for Railways (https://www.era.europa.eu/). It represents the concepts and relationships linked to the sectorial legal framework and the use cases under the Agency´s remit, as described in the Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) [to be updated after publication] on the common specifications for the register of railway infrastructure [to be updated after publication].


Currently, this Ontology covers the European railway infrastructure and the vehicle types authorized to operate over it. It is a semantic/browsable representation of the RINF application guide (1) and ERATV application guide (2) that were built by domain experts in the RINF and ERATV working parties.

The Ontology also includes the route book concepts described in appendix D2 \"Elements the infrastructure manager has to provide to the railway undertaking for the Route Book\" as presented in the Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) [to be updated after publication] 2019/773 of 16 May 2019 on the technical specification for interoperability relating to the operation and traffic management subsystem of the rail system within the European Union and [to be updated after publication] and the Appendix D3 [to be updated after publication]."""@en .

foaf:name rdfs:comment "A name for some thing."@en .

:XMLName rdfs:comment "Corresponding XML name as indicated in the RINF application guide"@en .

:affectedClass rdfs:comment "Annotation property used in SHACL shapes. Name of the classes that are the subject of properties that are being validated in a SHACL shape."@en .

:affectedProperty rdfs:comment "Annotation property used in SHACL shapes. Name of the properties that are being validated in a SHACL shape."@en .

:applicable rdfs:comment "Annotation used to point to the applicability of a parameter in RINF. Values are Y/N/NYA"@en .

:canonicalURI rdfs:comment """The canonical URI is defined for each instance of an Infrastructure element, e.g. section of line, operational point, track, tunnel, siding.
Objects of the infrastructure generated through RML mappings include (when provided) their validity start and end dates. With its identifier, plus all identifiers of its \"parent\" elements, and its validity dates, a hash URI is generated.
The canonical URI is the element's URI with its identifiers and without the validity dates. All of the hash URIs of an element point to its canonical URI.
Additionally, SoLs point to the canonical URIs of their start OP and end OP."""@en .

:shaclShapeValidationRule rdfs:comment "Annotation used to point to the SHACL shape that implements the validation for a certain RINF parameter (property). Each shape contains constraints for valid datatypes, patterns, min and max count, valid SKOS values and business rules."@en .

:InfrastructureElement rdfs:comment """This class encompasses all those classes that represent features that are  implemented in the European railway infrastructure. It is a subclass of the ERA Feature that has a spatial representation. It covers tracks, platforms, signals, tunnels, operational points, and sections of line.
A feature that belongs to the infrastructure can be abstracted (hasAbstraction) as a topological object. It also is related to the infrastructure manager through the property infrastructureMgr."""@en .

:dependencyNote rdfs:comment "This property is used to specify dependencies in natural language not covered by skos:scopeNote"@en .

:eratvIndex rdfs:comment "Index code used in the original definition of a parameter in ERATV."@en .

:formatNote rdfs:comment "This property is used to annotate in human readable the format of parameters"@en .

:hashSource rdfs:comment "This property indicates for each infrastructure element, the source, i.e. the identifier  or key that was input to the hash function in order to generate the hash value that is part of the hash URI."@en .

:inSkosConceptScheme rdfs:comment "Property that links an object SKOS property to the URI of the corresponding SKOS Concept Scheme."@en .

:legalDeadline rdfs:comment "Annotation used to point to legal obligation of a parameter in RINF"@en .

:rinfIndex rdfs:comment "Index code used in the original definition of a parameter in RINF."@en .

:scope rdfs:comment "Annotation property used in SHACL shapes. Indicates if the SHACL shape is validating a property of a specific instance (\"local\"), or if it needs to check other instances (\"global\"). For example, SHACL shape to validate no repeated ids within a specific track."@en .

:tentReference rdfs:comment "Used to annotate properties coming from the TenT regulations, to be used for monitoring the provision of the data."@en .

:tsiOPEAppendixD1Index rdfs:comment "The index of a vocabulary term in Appendix D1 Vehicle and train Route compatibility checks."@en .

:tsiOPEAppendixD2Index rdfs:comment "The index of a vocabulary term in Appendix D2 Elements the infrastructure manager has to provide to the railway undertaking for the Route Book from the document Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2019/773 of 16 May 2019 on the technical specification for interoperability relating to the operation and traffic management subsystem of the rail system within the European Union and repealing Decision 2012/757/EU."@en .

:tsiOPEAppendixD3Index rdfs:comment "The index of a vocabulary term in Appendix D3 ERTMS trackside engineering information relevant to operation that the infrastructure manager shall provide to the railway undertaking."@en .

:unitOfMeasure rdfs:comment "Magnitude of a quantity, defined and adopted by convention or by law, that is used as a standard for measurement of the same kind of quantity."@en .

:usedInRCCCalculations rdfs:comment "Indicates whether a RINF parameter is used in Route Compatibility Check calculations according to Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2019/773 of 16 May 2019 on the technical specification for interoperability relating to the operation and traffic management subsystem of the rail system within the European Union and repealing Decision."@en .

:TSIMagneticFields rdfs:comment "Indication whether rules exist and are compliant with the TSI."@en .

:tsiMagneticFields rdfs:comment "Indication whether rules exist and are compliant with the TSI."@en .

:TSITractionHarmonics rdfs:comment "Indication whether rules exist and are compliant with the TSI."@en .

:tsiTractionHarmonics rdfs:comment "Indication whether rules exist and are compliant with the TSI."@en .

:accelerationLevelCrossing rdfs:comment "Existence of limit for acceleration of train if stopping or recovering speed close to a level crossing expressed in a specific reference acceleration curve."@en .

:CommonCharacteristicsSubset rdfs:comment "A set of different infrastructure objects sharing the same common technical characteristics. The parameters may not be restricted to only one railway subsystem, but it can include common characteristics from each one of them (infrastructure, energy, track-side CCS)"@en .

:Track rdfs:comment "A pair of rails over which rail borne vehicles can run."@en .

:Document rdfs:comment "Document in any of the ERA systems, e.g. reference document in RINF."@en .

:additionalBrakingInformationDocument rdfs:comment "Electronic document available in two EU languages from the IM stored by the Agency providing additional information as defined in point (2) of point 4.2.2.6.2 of TSI OPE."@en .

:RunningTrack rdfs:comment "A running track means any track used for train service movements; passing loops and meeting loops on plain line or track connections only required for train operation are not published"@en .

:aggregates rdfs:comment "Specifies the linear elements aggregated by a non-linear element."@en .

:NonLinearElement rdfs:comment "Represents a non-linear element in the network."@en .

:LinearElement rdfs:comment "Pieces of tracks composing the topology"@en .

:allocationCompany rdfs:comment "The organisation in charge to allocate the code for the subsidiary location."@en .

:SubsidiaryLocation rdfs:comment "Subsidiary location must be linked to a Primary Location and specifies in more detailed way part, attributes, or usage of Primary location. It may be also a non-rail point or a rail point that is not managed by an Infrastructure Manager (IM). It may be defined by entity having company code according to their needs. The Subsidiary location is optional and dependent upon business needs."@en .

:OrganisationRole rdfs:comment "Represents an n-ary relationship between a Body and a role"@en .

:appliesToDirection rdfs:comment "The direction relative to the origin of the linear element towards the point reference applies."@en .

:NetPointReference rdfs:comment "Represents a point reference in the network."@en .

:atoCommunicationSystem rdfs:comment "Supported ATO communication systems from trackside."@en .

:atoGradeAutomation rdfs:comment "ATO grade of automation installed lineside."@en .

:etcsBaseline rdfs:comment "ETCS baseline installed lineside."@en .

:atoSystemVersion rdfs:comment "ATO system version according to the specification referenced in TSI CCS 2023/1695"@en .

:authorizedCountry rdfs:comment "Indicates the country(ies) in where a vehicle type has been authorized to operate."@en .

:VehicleType rdfs:comment """A vehicle type that has been authorized to operate on the EU railway infrastructure. Type means a vehicle type defining the basic design characteristics of the vehicle as covered by a type or design examination certificate described in the relevant verification module.

Basic design characteristics means the parameters that are used to identify the vehicle type as specified in the issued vehicle type authorisation and recorded in the European Register of Authorised Vehicle Types ('ERATV').

The above mentioned certificate should be documented using era:certificate.
"""@en .

:axleBearingConditionMonitoring rdfs:comment "Axle bearing condition monitoring."@en .

:belongsTo rdfs:comment "Indicates that an infrastructure element belongs to a certain subset that contains common characteristics."@en .

:contains rdfs:comment "Indicates that a subset with common characteristics contains a certain infrastructure element."@en .

:borderPointOf rdfs:comment "Relates the information that each country maintains on a border point, to the operational point that represents the general information on the border point."@en .

:opInfoPerCountry rdfs:comment "Relates an operational point that represents the general information of a border point to the information that each country maintains for the border point."@en .

:OperationalPoint rdfs:comment "An operational point (OP) means any location for train service operations, where train services may begin and end or change route, and where passenger or freight services may be provided; operational point also means any location at boundaries between Member States or infrastructure managers."@en .

:ReferenceBorderPoint rdfs:comment "List of reference border points that are specified in the RINF Application Guide."@en .

:referenceBorderPoint rdfs:comment "Relates an operational point that is a border point with an instance of the list of reference border points that are specified in the RINF Application Guide."@en .

:cantDeficiencyBasicSSP rdfs:comment "Essential information for railway undertakings with a worse (lower) tolerated cant deficiency than those for which the ETCS trackside provides SSP (Static Speed Profiles) in conjunction with parameter \"Other Cant Deficiency train categories for which the ETCS trackside is configured to provide SSP\"."@en .

:etcsLevelType rdfs:comment "ETCS application level related to the track side equipment."@en .

:otherCantDeficiencyBasicSSP rdfs:comment """Essential information for drivers of trains with a worse (lower) tolerated cant deficiency than those for which the ETCS trackside provides SSP (Static Speed Profiles) in conjunction with parameter \"Cant Deficiency used for the basic SSP\".
According to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]"""@en .

:carrierLinearElement rdfs:comment "The carrier linear element in relation to which the orientation is based on"@en .

:Orientation rdfs:comment "Represents the orientation of a railway object in relation to a carrier linear element. It can be described by direction, orientation and side."@en .

:category rdfs:comment "(Deprecated) Vehicle category."@en .

:vehicleCategory rdfs:comment "Indicates the core purpose of a railway vehicle: delivering traction, transporting goods or passengers or serving as a special vehicle."@en .

:certificate rdfs:comment """For this Vehicle Type (and its underlying authorisation cases),
- the type or design examination certificate (`era:CertificationLevelDocument`) described in the relevant verification module as issued by Notified Bodies, supporting the EC Declaration(s) of Verification for the subsystems in scope of the type's authorisation by an authorizing entity.
- a National certificate reference (`vpa:EvidenceDocument`)

Use only if no link can be made with the underlying authorisation and its presented certificates."""@en .

:Certificate rdfs:comment "Base class for those Certificates in the ERADIS register, which allow a IOD/SD described process."@en .

:companyCodeCategory rdfs:comment "Category of a Railway company. Can be Infrastructure, Freight or Passenger. Deprecated as it will be integrated with the Organisations properties."@en .

:compatibilityProcedureDocument rdfs:comment """Electronic document available in two EU languages from the IM stored by the Agency with:  
- precise procedures for the static and dynamic route compatibility checks;
Or
- relevant information for carrying out the checks for specific structures."""@en .

:conditionalRegenerativeBrake rdfs:comment "Indication whether regenerative braking is permitted, not permitted, or permitted under specific conditions."@en .

:ContactLineSystem rdfs:comment "System that is used to transmit electrical energy to road or rail vehicles."@en .

:contactLineSystemType rdfs:comment "Indication of the type of the contact line system."@en .

:conditionsAppliedRegenerativeBraking rdfs:comment "Name and/or reference of the document specifying the conditions applying in regards to regenerative braking."@en .

:conditionsSwitchClassBSystems rdfs:comment "Name and/or reference of the document specifying the Special technical conditions required to switch over between ERTMS/ETCS and Class B systems."@en .

:ETCS rdfs:comment "TSI compliant train protection system ERTMS / ETCS application level and baseline related to the track side equipment."@en .

:switchProtectControlWarning rdfs:comment "Indication whether a switch over between different systems whilst running exists."@en .

:conditionsUseReflectivePlates rdfs:comment "Details of any conditions for using the reflective plates on freight corridors. Specific case for Portugal and Spain until 1.1.2025 and Belgium and France until 1.1.2026."@en .

:connectedTo rdfs:comment "Represents a bidirectional connection between two Track instances."@en .

:NetElement rdfs:comment "It is a representation of all building blocks of the topology. It references an associated topological network element."@en .

:NetRelation rdfs:comment "Defines a relation between two elements."@en .

:contactLineSystem rdfs:comment "System that is used to transmit electrical energy to road or rail vehicles."@en .

:contactStripMaterial rdfs:comment "Indication of which contact strip materials are permitted to be used on the infrastructure or with which the vehicles (of the VehicleType) may be equipped with."@en .

:dataGSMRNetwork rdfs:comment "Data SIM Card GSM-R Home Network."@en .

:dataRadioCompatible rdfs:comment "Radio requirements used for demonstrating technical compatibility data."@en .

:definesSubset rdfs:comment "(deprecated) not in use anymore. For the purposes of the register of infrastructure, each infrastructure manager may describe its railway network optionally via common characteristic subsets."@en .

:InfrastructureManager rdfs:comment "(deprecated) The infrastructure manager owns and operates the railway network and related infrastructure."@en .

:direction rdfs:comment "The direction of the orientation of a railway element, in relation to the carrier linear element"@en .

:documentRestrictionPositionContactLineSeparation rdfs:comment "Name and/or reference of the document specifying the restriction(s) related to the position of Multiple Traction unit(s) to comply with contact line separation."@en .

:documentRestrictionPowerConsumption rdfs:comment "Name and/or reference of the document specifying the restriction(s) related to power consumption of specific electric traction unit(s)."@en .

:eddyCurrentBraking rdfs:comment "Indication of limitations on the use of eddy current brakes."@en .

:eddyCurrentBrakingConditionsDocument rdfs:comment "Electronic document available in two EU languages from the IM stored by the Agency with conditions for the use of eddy current brakes identified in 1.1.1.1.6.2."@en .

:elementA rdfs:comment """References the first topological element in an oriented relation.
For example, it may indicate the object that corresponds to a section of line, an operational point or a track inside an operational point connected at start."""@en .

:elementB rdfs:comment """References the second topological linear element in an oriented relation.
For example, it may indicate the object that corresponds to a section of line, an operational point or a track inside an operational point connected at end."""@en .

:elementPart rdfs:comment "References the topology object of a higher-granularity level which contains a lower-granularity topology object."@en .

:endCouplingType rdfs:comment "Type of end coupling (indicating tensile and compressive forces)."@en .

:endLocation rdfs:comment "Geographical coordinates in decimal degrees and km of the line at the end of a tunnel."@en .

geosparql:hasGeometry rdfs:comment """
      A spatial representation for a given feature.
    """@en .

:Tunnel rdfs:comment "A railway tunnel is an excavation or a construction around the track provided to allow the railway to pass for example higher land, buildings or water."@en .

:endsAt rdfs:comment "Specifies the ending point of a linear reference."@en .

:NetLinearReference rdfs:comment "Represents a linear reference in the network."@en .

:energySupplySystem rdfs:comment "Indication of the traction supply system (nominal voltage and frequency)."@en .

:errorCorrectionsOnboard rdfs:comment "List of unacceptable errors impacting the IM network that are required to be solved in the on-board according to the TSI CCS point 7.2.10.3 specification maintenance point (ETCS, GSM-R and/or ATO). An additional parameter (era:errorCorrectionsOnboardExplanation) must document if a non-implemented CR has been accepted by the IM."@en .

:gsmrErrorCorrectionsOnboard rdfs:comment """List of unacceptable errors impacting the IM network that are required to be solved in the on-board according to the CCS TSI point 7.2.10.3 specification maintenance point.
The reason for deprecation is that this parameter does not appear in the latest legal text."""@en .

:etcs rdfs:comment "European Train Control System (ETCS) application level supported by the track side equipment."@en .

:etcsDegradedSituation rdfs:comment "ERTMS / ETCS application level for degraded situation related to the track side equipment."@en .

:etcsEquipmentOnBoardLevel rdfs:comment "ETCS equipment on-board and its level."@en .

:etcsInfill rdfs:comment "Information about installed trackside equipment capable to transmit infill information by loop or Global System for Mobile communications for Railways (GSM-R) for level 1 installations."@en .

:etcsMVersion rdfs:comment "ETCS M_version according to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C], SRS 7.5.1.79."@en .

:etcsSystemCompatibility rdfs:comment "ETCS requirements used for demonstrating technical compatibility."@en .

:etcsTransmittedTrackConditions rdfs:comment "Transmittable track conditions by the CCSSubsystem, according to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]"@en .

:gsmRActiveMobiles rdfs:comment "Number of simultaneous communication session on board for ETCS level 2 required for a smooth running of the train. This relates to the radio block centre (RBC) handling of communication sessions. Not safety critical and no matter of interoperability."@en .

:rbcID rdfs:comment "Unique RBC identification (NID_C+NID_RBC)  as defined in the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C] (TSI CCS)."@en .

:rbcPhone rdfs:comment "Unique RBC calling number (NID_RADIO) as defined in the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]."@en .

:etcsNationalPacket44Function rdfs:comment "Indication whether data for national applications is transmitted between track and train."@en .

:etcsNationalPacket44 rdfs:comment "Indication whether data for national applications is transmitted between track and train."@en .

:etcsRestrictionsConditionsDoc rdfs:comment "Indication of the document where restrictions or conditions due to partial compliance with the TSI CCS are described."@en .

:europeanTransportCorridor rdfs:comment "Indication of which European Transport Corridor the element belongs to."@en .

:TENTCorridor rdfs:comment "Represents the TEN-T network classification of an element, including its network level, type of traffic, and associated European transport corridors."@en .

:fireSafetyCategory rdfs:comment "Fire safety category for tunnels."@en .

:freightCorridor rdfs:comment "Indication whether the line is designated to a Railway Freight Corridor."@en .

:frenchTrainDetectionSystemLimitation rdfs:comment "Specific for route compatibility check on French network. The reason for deprecation is because of replacement by a class, an object property and two datatype properties. The reason is that the property is composed of two values: A boolean [Y/N] and  a number N is between 1 and 8."@en .

:TrainDetectionSystem rdfs:comment "Safety system used to detect the presence of vehicles on the railway track."@en .

:frenchTrainDetectionSystemLimitationApplicable rdfs:comment "Part of the section with train detection limitation that indicates if it is applicable. Only for the French network."@en .

:frenchTrainDetectionSystemLimitationNumber rdfs:comment """Part of the section with train detection limitation that indicates the type of train detection limitation.

Specific for route compatibility check on French network.

Sections with:
[1] Tonnage circulated per track is inferior to 15000 tons/day/track
[2] Directional Interlocking
[3] 45-second delay for directional interlocking
[4] Installation with track circuit announcement
[5] Absence of a shunting assistance pedal in the normal direction of circulation for non-reversible double track lines
[6] Absence of a shunting assistance pedal regardless of the direction of traffic for single track lines and tracks for two way working
[7] Absence of a pedal announcement mechanism
[8] 45-second delay for specific announcement reset devices"""@en .

:tdsFrenchTrainDetectionSystemLimitation rdfs:comment "Specific for route compatibility check on French network."@en .

:FrenchTrainDetectionSystemLimitation rdfs:comment "Specific for route compatibility check on French network."@en .

:frequencyBandsForDetection rdfs:comment "Bands of the frequency management of the train detection systems as defined in the TSI CCS, and in the specific cases or technical documents referred to in Article 13 of TSI CCS when they are available."@en .

:maximumInterferenceCurrent rdfs:comment "Maximum interference current limits allowed for track circuits for a defined frequency band."@en .

:minVehicleImpedance rdfs:comment "Impedance as defined in the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [D]"@en .

:tdsMaximumMagneticField rdfs:comment """The maximum magnetic field limits allowed for axle counters (in dB µA/m) for a defined frequency band.
It should be provided in 3 directions."""@en .

:gaugingProfile rdfs:comment "Gauges as defined in European standard or other local gauges, including lower or upper part."@en .

:gaugingTransversalDocument rdfs:comment "Electronic document available from the IM stored by the Agency with the transversal section of the particular points requiring specific checks due to deviations from gauging referred to in parameter \"Gauging\". Where relevant, guidance for the check with the particular point may be attached to the document with the transversal section."@en .

:gsmRAdditionalInfo rdfs:comment "Any additional information on network characteristics or corresponding document available from the IM and stored by the Agency, e.g.; interference level, leading to the recommendation of additional on-board protection."@en .

:gprsForETCS rdfs:comment "Indication if GPRS can be used for ETCS"@en .

:gsmROptionalFunctions rdfs:comment "Use of optional GSM-R functions which might improve operation on the line. They are for information only and not for network access criteria."@en .

:gsmRRadioDataCommunication rdfs:comment "GSM-R Radio Data communication on board and its Baseline."@en .

:gsmRVersion rdfs:comment "GSM-R functional requirements specification (FRS) and system requirements specification (SRS) in accordance with the specification respectively referenced in Appendix A-1, index [E] and index [F], version number or baseline installed."@en .

:gsmrConstraintsOperateOnlyInCircuitSwitch rdfs:comment "These constraints, where applicable, are meant to manage the limited number of circuit-switched radio connections that can be handled simultaneously by a Radio Block Center."@en .

:gsmrNetworkCoverage rdfs:comment "Name of the own GSM-R network and list of GSM-R networks which are covered by a roaming agreement (for CS services)."@en .

:hasAbstraction rdfs:comment "Property that links a physical entity with its topological abstraction representation."@en .

:hasImplementation rdfs:comment "Property that links a topological abstraction entity with its physical representation."@en .

:hasLRS rdfs:comment "Specifies the linear referencing system to which the kilometre post is referenced. The linear referencing system is commonly the main railway line and it provides the framework for identifying the post's location along the railway line, using distance measurements rather than geographical coordinates."@en .

:KilometricPost rdfs:comment "Represents a kilometric post in the linear positioning system."@en .

:LinearPositioningSystem rdfs:comment """Represents a linear positioning system used for referencing positions on the network.
It can also represent a sequence of one or more sections of line, used for regular railway operations."""@en .

:hasLrsCoordinate rdfs:comment "Specifies the LRS coordinate associated with a topological coordinate."@en .

:LinearPositioningSystemCoordinate rdfs:comment "Represents coordinates in a linear positioning system."@en .

:hasOrganisationRole rdfs:comment "Relates the Organisation role instance (the role played by an Organisation)  with the specific role in the taxonomy of organisation roles."@en .

:Signal rdfs:comment "A railway signal is a visual display device (next to the tracks or via a DMI in the cabin) that conveys instructions or provides advance warning of instructions regarding the driver's authority to proceed."@en .

:hasPart rdfs:comment """Indicates that an infrastructure element is composed of one or more other (distinct) infrastructure elements.
This property is used to represent part-whole relationships between infrastructure elements.
An element cannot be a part of itself."""@en .

:isPartOf rdfs:comment """Indicates that an infrastructure element is a part of another (distinct) infrastructure element.
An element cannot be part of itself.
This property is the inverse of era:hasPart and represents the partial or whole-part relationship between infrastructure elements."""@en .

:siding rdfs:comment "Reference to a related siding."@en .

:track rdfs:comment "Reference to a related railway track."@en .

:hasSequence rdfs:comment "The ordered sequence of topological linear elements which create a linear net reference."@en .

:hasTopoCoordinate rdfs:comment "Specifies the topological coordinate of a network point reference."@en .

:TopologicalCoordinate rdfs:comment "Represents a topological coordinate."@en .

:hotAxleBoxDetectorDirection rdfs:comment "Direction of measurement of trackside HABD, specific for the French Italian and Swedish networks."@en .

:HABD rdfs:comment """A trackside Hot Axle Box Detector (HABD), necessary for the route compatibility check.
Specific for the French, Italian and Swedish networks"""@en .

:inCountry rdfs:comment "Indicates the country in which an entity resides."@en .

:inNUTS3 rdfs:comment "Reference to NUTS-3 place or city"@en .

:PrimaryLocation rdfs:comment """Primary Location is a place used by IM to define a path for a train in TAF/TAP TSI framework/messages. This location is a rail point inside the rail network where train starts, ends, stops, or runs through or change line. This location must be managed by an Infrastructure Manager (IM) identified by company code.

Primary locations are identified by single and unique Primary Location codes. Primary location code is allocated based on processes defined by national entity. Primary location codes are used in any kind of TAF/TAP communication.
"""@en .

:includes rdfs:comment "List of linear references included in an network area reference."@en .

:NetAreaReference rdfs:comment "Represents an area reference in the network."@en .

:infrastructureManager rdfs:comment "Relates a subset with common characteristics with its IM, represented by an instance of organisation role that points to the \"infrastructure manager\" concept in the taxonomy."@en .

:infrastructureMgr rdfs:comment "(deprecated) not in use. Relates any feature implemented in the European railway infrastructure with its infrastructure manager."@en .

:instructionsSwitchRadioSystems rdfs:comment "Name and/or reference of the document specifying the Special instructions to switch over between different radio systems."@en .

:kmPost rdfs:comment "The closest kilometric post on the line, used as a reference by the LRS coordinate."@en .

:legacyRadioSystem rdfs:comment "Indication of radio legacy systems installed."@en .

:lineCategory rdfs:comment "Classification of a line according to the TSI INF"@en .

:lineNationalId rdfs:comment "Unique line identification or unique line number within Member State."@en .

:LineReference rdfs:comment "A reference to a specific railway line."@en .

:SectionOfLine rdfs:comment "A section of line means the part of line between adjacent operational points and may consist of several tracks."@en .

:NationalRailwayLine rdfs:comment """Railway line within a member state.
A line is a sequence of one or more sections of line, which connects operational points and which may consist of several tracks used for regular railway operation."""@en .

:nationalLine rdfs:comment """Indicates a relationship with a national railway line at a specific kilometer point.
For a Section of Line: unique line identification or unique line number within Member State."""@en .

:lineReference rdfs:comment "Indicates a relationship with a national railway line at a specific kilometer point."@en .

:lineReferenceTunnelEnd rdfs:comment """Part of the End of tunnel that indicates the km of the line at the end of a tunnel.

The End of tunnel is the Geographical coordinates in decimal degrees and km of the line at the end of a tunnel."""@en .

:tunnelKilometerEnd rdfs:comment """Part of the End of tunnel that indicates the km of the line at the end of a tunnel.
The End of tunnel is the Geographical coordinates in decimal degrees and km of the line at the end of a tunnel. The reason for deprecation is that the property is now a subproperty of lineReference in order to represent the kilometer in relation to a national railway line"""@en .

:lineReferenceTunnelStart rdfs:comment """Part of the Start of tunnel that indicates the km of the line at the beginning of a tunnel.

The Start of tunnel is the Geographical coordinates in decimal degrees and km of the line at the beginning of a tunnel."""@en .

:linesideDistanceIndication rdfs:comment "Indication of types of appearance of track lineside distance indications."@en .

:LinesideDistanceIndication rdfs:comment """Frequency, appearance and positioning of a sign indicating distance as reference post. Two types of signs are normally available: kilometre post and hectometre post.
- A kilometre post is a lineside sign indicating the distance from a specific point, usually being the starting point of the railway line.
- A hectometre post is a lineside sign indicating a relative distance."""@en .

:linesideDistanceIndicationAppearance rdfs:comment "Indication of types of appearance of track lineside distance indications."@en .

:linesideDistanceIndicationPositioning rdfs:comment "Indication of the side along the track where the lineside indication is positioned (left or right, or both sides)."@en .

:linkedToPrimaryLocation rdfs:comment "Relates a subsidiary location with a primary location."@en .

:loadCapability rdfs:comment "A combination of the line category and speed at the weakest point of the track. The reason for deprecation is that the load capability property 1.1.1.1.2.4 was defined incorrectly as a SKOS property. It is composed of two values: (1)  line category, and (2) speed. Only line category is a list of predefined values (SKOS), whereas speed is an integer (according to the RINF application guide)."@en .

:LoadCapability rdfs:comment """A combination of the line category and speed at the weakest point of the track. 
Each track can have several load capability (structured) values, and each one has values for load model line category and load model speed."""@en,
    "This class together with properties loadCapabilityLineCategory and loadCapabilitySpeed replaces the previous loadCapability SKOS property."@en .

:loadCapabilityLineCategory rdfs:comment """Part of the load capability of a track that corresponds to the line category of the load model. 
The load capability is a value selected from the list of load models representing the line category which is amended by value of speed [km/h] permitted for a specific load model. The list of values may also be Route Availability which is amended by value of speed [miles/h] permitted for a specific load model."""@en .

:loadCapabilitySpeed rdfs:comment "Part of the load capability of a track that corresponds to the speed of the load model"@en .

:trackLoadCapability rdfs:comment "Relates the track with the class LoadCapability. A combination of the line category and speed at the weakest point of the track."@en .

:localRulesOrRestrictionsDoc rdfs:comment "Electronic document available from the IM stored by the Agency providing additional information."@en .

:lrsMethod rdfs:comment "The preferred line referencing system."@en .

:mNvcontact rdfs:comment """On-Board system reaction when T_NVCONTACT expires
According to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]"""@en .

:magneticBraking rdfs:comment "Indication of limitations on the use of magnetic brakes."@en .

:magneticBrakingConditionsDocument rdfs:comment "Electronic document available in two EU languages from the IM stored by the Agency with conditions for the use of magnetic brakes identified in 1.1.1.1.6.3."@en .

:manufacturer rdfs:comment "Vehicle manufacturer company."@en .

:Manufacturer rdfs:comment "(deprecated) Replaced by the era:Body class and era:manufacturer property. A company or organization that manufactures vehicles."@en .

:manufacturingCountry rdfs:comment "Indicates the country in which a vehicle or vehicle type is manufactured."@en .

:Vehicle rdfs:comment "A specific vehicle or wagon able and allowed to operate over railway infrastructure."@en .

:maxSandingOutput rdfs:comment """Maximum amount of sand accepted on the track within value of sanding output for 30s, given in grams.
Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777."""@en .

:minAxleLoadVehicleCategory rdfs:comment "Represents the category of vehicle which is amended by value of minimum permitted axle load [tonnes] (property minAxleLoad)."@en .

:MinVehicleImpedance rdfs:comment """Impedance as defined in the TSI CCS (Annex I, Appendix A, Table A.2 -Index 77).

Minimum vehicle impedance (between wheels and pantograph) (only for vehicles equipped for 1500V or 3000V DC).

Per Voltage:
[1500]: [CCCC]+[ZZZZ], with input capacitance [CCCC](Cin) and input impedance [ZZZZ](Zin)
[3000]: [CCCC]+[ZZZZ], idem."""@en .

:trainDetectionSystemType rdfs:comment "Indication of types of train detection systems installed."@en .

:minimumVerticalRadius rdfs:comment "Radius of the smallest vertical curve expressed in metres."@en .

:navigability rdfs:comment "Indicates the navigation possibilities between two related topological linear elements."@en .

:netElement rdfs:comment """References an associated topological object.
The reason for deprecating this property is that it is defined as \"References an associated topological object.\" and the vocabulary has already a property \"hasAbstraction\" which relates the implementation layer with the topological layer, https://citnet.tech.ec.europa.eu/CITnet/confluence/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=1122974879."""@en .

:netReference rdfs:comment "The reference that a physical infrastructure element has it on the topology. It may be used to define the positioning or a representation as a point, line or area"@en .

:NetBasicReference rdfs:comment "Basic positioning reference within the ERA ontology. It represents different types of geographical locations. Geographical coordinates are provided according to the standard World Geodetic System (WGS84)."@en .

:notApplicable rdfs:comment "Reference to a property that is not applicable."@en .

:notYetAvailable rdfs:comment "Reference to a property that is not provided."@en .

:ofParameter rdfs:comment "Indicates the parameter (object or datatype property) for which an applicability is being defined."@en .

:ParameterApplicability rdfs:comment "Applicability interval defines the date interval in which a characteristic of an infrastructure element is applicable. This interval can be applied for any of the technical characteristics or general information of infrastructure elements. This helps identifying planned changes applied to technical parameters over time."@en .

:onElement rdfs:comment "Specifies the linear element a section belongs to."@en .

:LinearElementSection rdfs:comment "Represents a section of a linear element."@en .

:onLinearElement rdfs:comment "Specifies the linear element a coordinate is associated with."@en .

:opEnd rdfs:comment "Operational point at the end of section of line (kilometres increasing from start OP to the end OP)."@en .

:opStart rdfs:comment "Operational point at the start of section of line (kilometres increasing from start OP to the end OP)."@en .

:opType rdfs:comment "Type of facility in relation to the dominating operational functions."@en .

:operatingLanguage rdfs:comment "The language or languages used in daily operation by infrastructure manager and published in its Network Statement, for the communication of operational or safety related messages between the staff of the infrastructure manager and the railway undertaking."@en .

:operationalRegimeType rdfs:comment "Double track type."@en .

:operationalRestriction rdfs:comment "Indicates an operational restriction of vehicle or wagon. Parking brake type (if the vehicle is fitted with it)."@en .

:osmClass rdfs:comment "Additional concept class according to OpenStreetMap."@en .

:otherPantographHead rdfs:comment "Indication of pantograph heads which are allowed to be used."@en .

:otherTrainProtection rdfs:comment "Indication of existence of other system than ETCS for degraded situation."@en .

:parameterApplicability rdfs:comment "Relates an infrastructure element or a common characteristics subset with the applicability of a certain parameter."@en .

:parameterValueType rdfs:comment "In the case of a change in the value of a parameter, there needs to be an information on the type of the new value. The “Value type” will have different possible options: “nominal”, “planned temporary restriction”, “permanent restriction”, “planned temporary closure”."@en .

:parkingBrakeType rdfs:comment "Parking brake type (if the vehicle is fitted with it)."@en .

:partOfTENT rdfs:comment "Links an element to its TEN-T network classification, which includes network level, type of traffic, and European transport corridor information."@en .

:passesThroughTunnel rdfs:comment "References a tunnel that a track goes through."@en .

:platformEdge rdfs:comment "Reference to a related platform edge."@en .

:PlatformEdge rdfs:comment "Platform for the purpose of RINF is understood as a platform edge. A platform concerns only the part of the structure neighbouring to the track (interfaced with trains)."@en .

:platformHeight rdfs:comment "Distance between the upper surface of platform and running surface of the neighbouring track. It is the nominal value expressed in millimetres."@en .

:positionOnA rdfs:comment "Determines the position of the topological object A in a relation."@en .

:positionOnB rdfs:comment "Determines the position of the topological object B in a relation."@en .

:previousVehicleType rdfs:comment "Denotes a previous VehicleType."@en .

:primaryLocation rdfs:comment "Primary location code developed for information exchange in accordance with the TSIs relating to the telematics applications subsystem."@en .

:tafTAPCode rdfs:comment "Not used anymore. It has been replaced by era:primaryLocationCode."@en,
    "Primary location code developed for information exchange in accordance with the TSIs relating to the telematics applications subsystem"@en .

:profileNumberSemiTrailers rdfs:comment "Coding for combined transport for semi-trailers (for all freight and mixed-traffic lines) in accordance with the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [B]."@en .

:profileNumberSwapBodies rdfs:comment "Coding for combined transport with swap bodies (for all freight and mixed-traffic lines) in accordance with the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [B]"@en .

:protectionLegacySystem rdfs:comment "Indication of which class B system is installed."@en .

:qNvdriverAdhes rdfs:comment """Qualifier determining whether the driver is allowed to modify the adhesion factor used by the ETCS on-board to calculate the braking curves.
According to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]"""@en .

:qNvemrrls rdfs:comment """Qualifier defining whether the application of the emergency brake for reasons other than a trip can be revoked as soon as the conditions for it have disappeared or after the train has come to a complete standstill.
According to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]"""@en .

:quieterRoutesExemptedCountry rdfs:comment "Country where a vehicle may operate without noise restrictions."@en .

:railInclination rdfs:comment "An angle defining the inclination of the head of a rail relative to the running surface."@en .

:reasonsEtcsRadioBlockCenterReject rdfs:comment "List of cases subject to system design choices made by the infrastructure manager according to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]"@en .

:RadioBlockCenter rdfs:comment """ETCS trackside centralised unit controlling ETCS train movements in level 2.

A centralised safety unit that receives train position information via radio and sends movement authorities via radio to trains."""@en .

:role rdfs:comment "Indicates the relationship of a Body to the organisation roles that it can play."@en .

:roleOf rdfs:comment "Indicates the corresponding Body that plays a certain organisation role."@en .

:Body rdfs:comment "Is an organisation or a physical person"@en .

:rollingStockFireCategory rdfs:comment "Categorisation how a passenger train with a fire on board will continue to operate for a defined time period"@en,
    "Passenger train fire category in accordance with point 4.1.4 of TSI LOC&PAS."@en .

:safeConsistLengthInformationNecessary rdfs:comment "Indication whether safe consist train length information from on-board is required to access the line for safety reasons and the required safety integrity level."@en .

:side rdfs:comment "Indication of the position of the signal in relation to the track in the running direction from the origin of the referencing system (e.g., direction of the main line)"@en .

:signalOrientation rdfs:comment "Relative position to the line of reference, given in km and indication if the signal refers to normal or opposite track direction"@en .

:signalId rdfs:comment "Identifier of signal."@en .

:signalType rdfs:comment "Signalling information for Route Book compilation. This list shall include fixed signals that protect danger points"@en .

:snowIceHailConditions rdfs:comment "Snow, ice and hail conditions."@en .

:solNature rdfs:comment "Kind of section of line expressing size of presented data which depends on fact whether it connects OPs generated by division of a big node into several OPs or not."@en .

:specialAreaType rdfs:comment "Indicates the special area or location types such as safe areas and restricted area types."@en .

:SpecialArea rdfs:comment """Non-stopping Area: Area defined by the Infrastructure Manager where it may not be safe or suitable to stop a train.
Safe Area: Area defined by the Infrastructure Manager where it is safe or suitable to stop and evacuate a train.
Industrial Risk Area: locations where it is dangerous for the driver to step out."""@en .

:specialTunnelArea rdfs:comment "Relates a tunnel with a special area or location."@en .

:SpecialTunnelArea rdfs:comment """Area or location within a tunnel:
- a safe area: a walkway, evacuation and rescue points, with the location value provided as Kilometric point of the start;
- a restricted area (non-stopping area or industrial risk location in a tunnel);
- an area with special passing protocols"""@en .

:standardCombinedTransportContainers rdfs:comment "Coding for combined transport for containers (for all freight and mixed-traffic lines) in accordance with the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [B]"@en .

:standardCombinedTransportRollerUnits rdfs:comment "Coding for combined transport for roller units (for all freight and mixed-traffic lines) in accordance with the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [B]"@en .

:startLocation rdfs:comment """Part of the Start of tunnel that indicates the Geographical coordinates according to the standard World Geodetic System (WGS). Precision for both geographical latitude and geographical longitude is assumed as [NN.NNNNNNN] in degrees with decimals what gives discretion of 10 cm in the network.
The Start of tunnel is the Geographical coordinates in decimal degrees and km of the line at the beginning of a tunnel."""@en .

:startsAt rdfs:comment "Specifies the starting point of a linear reference."@en .

:state rdfs:comment "Denoting the state of the certificate/declaration. Can be in one of the following: Amended, New, Suspended, Withdrawn."@en .

:subCategory rdfs:comment "(Deprecated) Vehicle subcategory."@en .

:vehicleSubCategory rdfs:comment "Indicates the further classification (but not any family/platform) of vehicles within a vehicle category."@en .

:subsetOf rdfs:comment "Relates a subset with common characteristics with another subset with common characteristics."@en .

:subsidiaryLocationType rdfs:comment "Indicates the subsidiary location type that belongs to a taxonomy."@en .

:supportedPlatformHeight rdfs:comment "Platform height for which the vehicle is designed."@en .

:tdsMinAxleLoadVehicleCategory rdfs:comment "Indication of load given in tonnes depending of the category of vehicle."@en .

:temperatureRange rdfs:comment "Temperature range for unrestricted access to the line."@en .

:maximumTemperature rdfs:comment "Deprecated because both RINF and ERATV define a temperature range as a set of predefined values (see https://www.era.europa.eu/system/files/2023-04/iu-eratv_application_guide_for_register_2016-797_en_0.pdf). Maximum temperature allowed for unrestricted operation access, according to European standard."@en .

:minimumTemperature rdfs:comment "Deprecated because both RINF and ERATV define a temperature range as a set of predefined values (see https://www.era.europa.eu/system/files/2023-04/iu-eratv_application_guide_for_register_2016-797_en_0.pdf). Minimum temperature allowed for unrestricted operation access, according to European standard."@en .

:tenClassification rdfs:comment "Indication of the part of the trans-European network the infrastructure element belongs to."@en .

:tentNetworkLevel rdfs:comment "Classification of the element according to its level in the Trans-European Transport Network (TEN-T)."@en .

:thermalCapacityTSIReference rdfs:comment "Reference case of a TSI thermal capacity."@en .

:trackDirection rdfs:comment """The normal running direction is:
- the same as the direction defined by the start and end of the SoL: (N)
- the opposite to the direction defined by the start and end of the SoL: (O)
- both directions: (B)"""@en .

:trackPhaseInfo rdfs:comment "Relates the Track with PhaseInfo. Indication of required several information on phase separation."@en .

:PhaseInfo rdfs:comment "Indication of required several information on phase separation."@en .

:trackRaisedPantographsDistanceAndSpeed rdfs:comment "Indication of maximum number of raised pantographs per train allowed and minimum spacing centre line to centre line of adjacent pantograph heads, expressed in metres, at the given speed."@en .

:RaisedPantographsDistanceAndSpeed rdfs:comment """Indication of maximum number of raised pantographs per train allowed and minimum spacing centre line to centre line of adjacent pantograph heads, expressed in metres, at the given speed.
Each track can have several raised pantographs per train allowed (structured) values, and each one has values for number of pantographs, minimum distance between pantographs, in metres, and speed considered in km/h."""@en .

:trackSystemSeparationInfo rdfs:comment "Indication of required several information on system separation"@en .

:SystemSeparationInfo rdfs:comment "Indication of required several information on system separation."@en .

:systemSeparationInfo rdfs:comment """(deprecated) Indication of required several information on system separation.
Deprecated because of replacement by four properties. The reason is that the property is composed of four values: length [NNN], the length of the system separation in metres; switch off breaker [Y/N]. Single selection of 'Y=yes' or 'N=no' to show whether the breaker has to be switched off;  lower pantograph [Y/N]. Single selection of 'Y=yes' or 'N=no' to show whether the pantograph has to be lowered, and [CharacterString]  to show whether the supply system has to be changed."""@en .

:tracksideHabd rdfs:comment "Link between the running track and the HABD, covering the RINF parameters 1.1.1.1.7.(5-9)"@en .

:trainDetectionSystem rdfs:comment "Technical characteristics of the train detection systems installed in the section of line."@en .

:trainDetectionSystemSpecificCheck rdfs:comment "Reference to the technical specification of train detection system, in accordance with the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [D]"@en .

:trainDetectionSystemSpecificCheckDocument rdfs:comment "Electronic document from the IM stored by the Agency with precise values in accordance with TSI CCS Article13 and the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [D], for the specific check to be performed for train detection systems identified in parameter \"Type of track circuits or axle counters to which specific checks are needed\"."@en .

:tsiCompliantCompositeBrakeBlocks rdfs:comment "Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777. TSI compliance of rules on the use of composite brake blocks."@en .

:tsiCompliantFerromagneticWheel rdfs:comment "TSI compliance of Ferromagnetic characteristics of wheel material required. Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777."@en .

:tsiCompliantMaxDistConsecutiveAxles rdfs:comment "Indication whether required distance between two consecutive axles is compliant with the TSI. Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777."@en .

:tsiCompliantMaxImpedanceWheelset rdfs:comment "TSI compliance of maximum permitted impedance between opposite wheels of a wheelset. Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777."@en .

:tsiCompliantMetalConstruction rdfs:comment "TSI compliance of rules for vehicle metal construction. Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777."@en .

:tsiCompliantMetalFreeSpace rdfs:comment "TSI compliance of rules for metal-free space around wheels. Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777."@en .

:tsiCompliantRSTShuntImpedance rdfs:comment "TSI compliance of rules on combination of RST characteristics influencing shunting impedance. Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777."@en .

:tsiCompliantSandCharacteristics rdfs:comment "TSI Compliance of rules on sand characteristics. Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777."@en .

:tsiCompliantSanding rdfs:comment "TSI compliance of sanding rules to allow compatibility with track circuits. Too much sand brings the risk of not detecting trains in tracks equipped with track circuits. Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777."@en .

:tsiCompliantShuntDevices rdfs:comment "Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777. TSI compliance of rules on shunt assisting devices."@en .

:tsiPantographHead rdfs:comment "Indication of TSI compliant pantograph heads which are allowed to be used."@en .

:tunnelDocRef rdfs:comment "Electronic document available from the IM stored by the Agency with precise description of the clearance gauge and geometry of the tunnel."@en .

:typeOfTraffic rdfs:comment "Classification of the type of traffic carried on the element."@en .

:typeVersionId rdfs:comment """Indicates the registrationVersion with Ids 10, 20 and 30 indicating registration according to Directive 2008/57/EC and implementing Decision 2011/665/EU, and 40 and 50 indicating registration according to regime described in Directive 2008/57/EC.
The allowed values for this property belong to the SKOS Concept Scheme http://data.europa.eu/949/concepts/type-version-ids/TypeVersionIds."""@en .

:validity rdfs:comment "Relates a feature with a temporal feature to indicate a validity period."@en .

:Feature rdfs:comment "Class that encompasses the features that are part of the physical infrastructure (class InfrastructureElement) and the topological objects (class TopologicalObject). It is a subclass of the geographical Feature class that has a spatial representation."@en .

:TemporalFeature rdfs:comment "The union of TemporalDuration that represents a time extent and TemporalEntity that represents a temporal interval or instant."@en .

:vehicleKeeper rdfs:comment "Indicates the organization that owns/operated a vehicle or wagon."@en .

:VehicleKeeper rdfs:comment """The natural or legal person that, being the owner of a vehicle or having the right to use it,
exploits the vehicle as a means of transport and is registered as such in a vehicle register referred to in Article 47 of (EU)2016/797."""@en .

:vehicleType rdfs:comment "Indicates the vehicle type of a specific vehicle or wagon."@en .

:vehicleTypeMaximumSpeedAndCantDeficiency rdfs:comment "Relates the vehicle type with its values of maximum speed and cant deficiency."@en .

:MaximumSpeedAndCantDeficiency rdfs:comment "Combination of maximum speed and maximum cant deficiency for which the vehicle was assessed."@en .

:maximumSpeedAndCantDeficiency rdfs:comment """Combination of maximum speed and maximum cant deficiency for which the vehicle was assessed.

This property was before an object skos property. The values for this property do not come from a list of predefined values. Thus, the original object property was replaced by this datatype property with range xsd:string.
Deprecated because of replacement by a class and two integer properties. The reason is that the property represents two concepts: [number] km/h for maximum speed - [number] mm for maximum cant deficiency."""@en .

:vehicleTypesCompatibleTrafficLoad rdfs:comment "The infrastructure managers shall provide through RINF the information to the RU regarding list of vehicle types compatible with the route for which they have already verified compatibility for parameter Traffic load and load carrying capacity of infrastructure and train detection systems, where such information is available."@en .

:vehiclesCompatibleTrafficLoad rdfs:comment "The infrastructure managers shall provide through RINF the information or a document to the RU regarding list of vehicles compatible with the route for which they have already verified compatibility for parameter Traffic load and load carrying capacity of infrastructure and train detection systems, where such information is available."@en .

:voiceGSMRNetwork rdfs:comment "Voice SIM Card GSM-R Home Network"@en .

:voiceRadioCompatible rdfs:comment "Radio requirements used for demonstrating technical compatibility voice."@en .

:wheelSetGauge rdfs:comment "A single value expressed in millimetres that identifies the track gauge."@en .

:wheelSetGaugeChangeoverFacility rdfs:comment "Wheelset gauge changeover facility. The allowed values for this property belong to the SKOS Concept Scheme http://data.europa.eu/949/concepts/gauge-changeover-facilities/GaugeChangeoverFacilities"@en .

time:hasBeginning rdfs:comment "Beginning of a temporal entity"@en, "Comienzo de una entidad temporal."@es .

time:hasTime rdfs:comment "Proporciona soporte a la asociación de una entidad temporal (instante o intervalo) a cualquier cosa."@es,
    "Supports the association of a temporal entity (instant or interval) to any thing"@en .

time:hasEnd rdfs:comment "End of a temporal entity."@en, "Final de una entidad temporal."@es .

:altitudeRange rdfs:comment "Altitude range A1, A2 or A<integer> (integer era:altitudeRangeDetail)."@en .

:altitudeRangeDetail rdfs:comment "Altitude range value for 'X' if value 'AX' is selected in altitude range."@en .

:appliesInBothDirections rdfs:comment "Specifies if the section applies in both directions (optional)."@en .

:areaBoardingAid rdfs:comment "Information of the train access level for which the boarding aid can be used."@en .

:assistanceStartingTrain rdfs:comment "Indication of existence of equipment or staff supporting the train crew in starting the train."@en .

:atoErrorCorrectionsOnboard rdfs:comment "List of unacceptable errors impacting the IM network that are required to be solved in the on-board ATO according to the CCS TSI point 7.2.10.3 specification maintenance point."@en .

:automaticDroppingDeviceRequired rdfs:comment "Indication of whether an automatic dropping device (ADD) required on the vehicle."@en .

:axleSpacing rdfs:comment "Position of the axles along the unit. a: Distance between axles; b: Distance from end axle to the end of the nearest coupling plane; c: distance between two inside axles."@en .

:bigMetalMass rdfs:comment "Indication of existence of metal mass in the vicinity of the location, susceptible of perturbating the reading of balises by the on-board system."@en .

:boardingAids rdfs:comment "Description of any integrated boarding aids (if provided)."@en .

:borderPointId rdfs:comment "Border point identification in the list of reference border points in the RINF application guide."@en .

dcterms:identifier rdfs:comment "An unambiguous reference to the resource within a given context."@en .

:brakeWeightPercentage rdfs:comment "Brake weight percentage (lambda) or Braked mass."@en .

:cantDefficiency rdfs:comment "Cant deficiency (maximum uncompensated lateral acceleration) for which the vehicle has been assessed. For dual gauge vehicles values for each gauge have to be indicated."@en .

:cantDeficiency rdfs:comment "Maximum cant deficiency expressed in millimetres defined as difference between the applied cant and a higher equilibrium cant the line has been designed for."@en .

:catenaryMaxRatedCurrent rdfs:comment "Maximum rated current from the catenary (to be indicated for each electrical energy supply system the vehicle is equipped for), given in A."@en .

:complianceInfTsi rdfs:comment "Compliance of the tunnel with TSI INF at the maximum permitted speed"@en .

:conditionsChargingElectricEnergyStorage rdfs:comment "Conditions set by IMs according to a standardised document"@en .

:conditionsSwitchTrainProtectionSystems rdfs:comment "Conditions to switch over between different class B train protection, control and warning systems."@en .

:conditionsTrainFormation rdfs:comment "Conditions of use regarding train formation."@en .

:contactStripMaterialMetallicContent rdfs:comment "Indication of max. percentage of contact strip material Impregnated Carbon permitted to be used."@en .

:containerHandlingFlag rdfs:comment "Indicates whether a primary location is suitable for handling containers and loading or unloading of containers."@en .

:crossSectionArea rdfs:comment "Smallest cross section area in square metres of the tunnel"@en .

:currentLimitationRequired rdfs:comment "Indication of whether an on board current or power limitation function on vehicles is required."@en .

:dNvovtrp rdfs:comment "Maximum distance for overriding the train trip in metres, according to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]."@en .

:dNvpotrp rdfs:comment "Maximum distance for reversing in Post Trip mode in metres, according to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]."@en .

:dNvroll rdfs:comment """Parameter used by the ETCS on-board to supervise the distance allowed to be travelled under the roll-away protection and the reverse movement protection, in metres
According to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]"""@en .

:dangerousGoodsTankCode rdfs:comment "Dangerous goods for which the vehicle is suitable (tank code)."@en .

:demonstrationENE rdfs:comment "Unique number for EI declarations following the same format requirements as specified for EC declarations in Annex VII of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2019/250."@en .

:demonstrationINF rdfs:comment "Unique number for EI declarations following the same format requirements as specified for EC declarations in Annex VII of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2019/250."@en .

:demonstrationSRT rdfs:comment "Unique number for EI declarations following the same format requirements as specified for EC declarations in Annex VII of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2019/250."@en .

:designMassExceptionalPayload rdfs:comment "Design mass under exceptional payload."@en .

:designMassNormalPayload rdfs:comment "Design mass under normal payload."@en .

:designMassWorkingOrder rdfs:comment "Design mass in working order."@en .

:dieselThermalAllowed rdfs:comment "Indication whether it is allowed to use diesel or other thermal traction in the tunnel"@en .

:digitalSchematicOverview rdfs:comment "Diagrammatic representation of the operational point in Well Known Text polyline"@en .

:distSignToPhaseEnd rdfs:comment "Distance between the signboard authorizing the driver to  raise pantograph  or  close the circuit breaker  after passing the phase separation and the end of the phase separation section."@en .

:documentUrl rdfs:comment "URL that is used to download a document, e.g. url for a reference document in RINF."@en .

:drivingCabs rdfs:comment """Number of driving cabs.

For vehicle types without driving cabs, this property should not be used, or the number of driving cabs is to be set to zero (0)."""@en .

:emergencyBrake rdfs:comment "Stopping distance and deceleration profile for each load condition per design maximum speed."@en .

:endOffsetFromOrigin rdfs:comment "End offset of the section from the origin."@en .

:energySupplyMaxPower rdfs:comment "Maximum power (to be indicated for each energy supply system the vehicle is equipped for), given in kW."@en .

:energySupplySystemTSICompliant rdfs:comment "Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777. Indication if the traction supply system (nominal voltage and frequency) is fully compliant with TSI."@en .

:errorCorrectionsOnboardExplanation rdfs:comment "Explanation on why a mandatory onboard CR required to be solved in the on-board (ETCS, GSM-R and/or ATO) was accepted by the IM."@en .

:etcsDataCommApp rdfs:comment "Data communication application for ETCS implementation."@en .

:etcsImplementsLevelCrossingProcedure rdfs:comment "If the trackside does not implement any solution to cover non-protected LXs (which are normally protected by means of a technical system), then drivers will be required to comply with instructions received from other sources"@en .

:etcsInfillLineAccess rdfs:comment "Indication whether infill is required to access the line for safety reasons."@en .

:etcsNationalApplications rdfs:comment "ETCS national applications implemented (NID_XUSER of Packet 44)."@en .

:hasEtcsNationalPacket44 rdfs:comment "Indication whether data for national packet 44 applications is transmitted between track and train."@en .

:etcsOnBoardImplementation rdfs:comment "ETCS on-board implementation."@en .

:etcsOptionalFunctions rdfs:comment "Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777. Optional ETCS functions which might improve operation on the line."@en .

:etcsSystemFunctionalitiesNextFiveYears rdfs:comment "(Deprecated) List of ETCS system version 2.2 or 3.0 functionalities to be required in the next 5 years according to TSI CCS point 6.1.1.2 and Appendix G"@en .

:etcsTransmitsTrackConditions rdfs:comment """If the trackside does not provide Track Conditions, the driver will need to be informed about such conditions via alternative methods.
According to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]"""@en .

:exemptSpecialVehiclesFromATO rdfs:comment "Indicates whether special vehicles are exempted from the need to install ATO (Automatic Train Operation) for this infrastructure element."@en .

:exemptSpecialVehiclesFromETCS rdfs:comment "Indicates whether special vehicles are exempted from the need to install ETCS (European Train Control System) for this infrastructure element."@en .

:exemptSpecialVehiclesFromRMR rdfs:comment "Indicates whether special vehicles are exempted from the need to install RMR (Railway Mobile Radio) for this infrastructure element."@en .

:existBridgeWindRestriction rdfs:comment "Indicate, if there are any wind restrictions for a bridge."@en .

:Bridge rdfs:comment "It is a structure constructed for the exclusive purpose of carrying railroad traffic across an obstruction. It can be used for defining non-stopping areas, big metal mass, resistance to traffic load etc."@en .

:existOpeningHoursLimitation rdfs:comment "Indicate, if there are any opening hours of the section of a line or Tunnel or Bridge."@en .

:openingHoursLimitation rdfs:comment "Opening hours of the section of a line or tunnel or a bridge"@en .

:existRestrictedDangerousGood rdfs:comment "Indicate, if there are any limits on transportation of dangerous goods."@en .

:restrictedDangerousGood rdfs:comment "Description of the type of dangerous good that are not allowed in the tunnel"@en .

:existRestrictedPeriodOfTimeDangerousGood rdfs:comment "Indicate, if there are any limits on specific time of a day for transport of dangerous goods."@en .

:restrictedPeriodOfTimeDangerousGood rdfs:comment "Describes the period of time for which the transport of dangerous goods is not allowed in the Section of Line"@en .

:existRestrictedTypeOfVehicleOfTunnel rdfs:comment "Indicate, if there are any limits on specific type of vehicle in the tunnel."@en .

:restrictedTypeOfVehicleInTunnel rdfs:comment "Specific types of vehicles restricted in the tunnel."@en .

:existTrainExclusionOfSimultaneity rdfs:comment "Indicate, if passenger and freight trains meeting together in a tunnel is allowed"@en .

:existenceOfIndustrialRisk rdfs:comment "Indication that the full section of line (or a part of it) it is identified by the Infrastructure Managers (and communicated to the RU) where drivers are not supposed to get off the locomotive."@en .

:fixedSeats rdfs:comment "Number of fixed seats (min to max number)."@en .

:flangeLubeForbidden rdfs:comment "Indication whether the use of on-board device for flange lubrication is forbidden."@en .

:flangeLubeRules rdfs:comment "Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777. Indication whether rules for activation or deactivation of flange lubrication exist."@en .

:freightFlag rdfs:comment "Indicates whether a freight train can perform commercial freight activity at a primary location."@en .

:gaugingCheckLocation rdfs:comment "Location of particular points requiring specific checks due to deviations from gauging referred to in parameter \"Gauging\""@en .

:gprsImplementationArea rdfs:comment "Indication of the area in which GPRS can be used for ETCS, expressed as a list of GPRS-enabled RBCs."@en .

:gradient rdfs:comment "Maximum value of the gradient for stabling tracks expressed in millimetres per metre."@en .

:gradientProfile rdfs:comment "Sequence of gradient values and locations of change in gradient"@en .

:gsmRNoCoverage rdfs:comment "Indication if there is no GSMR coverage"@en .

:gsmRSetsInDrivingCab rdfs:comment "Number of GSM-R mobile sets in driving cab for data transmission."@en .

:gsmrForcedDeregistrationFunctionalNumber rdfs:comment "This feature will determine the applicable operational rules for drivers and signallers when dealing with cab radios registered under wrong numbers."@en .

:handoverPointFlag rdfs:comment "Indicates whether a primary location is a point where legal responsibility changes between Infrastructure Managers. This can be, but does not have to be, in conjunction with a state border."@en .

:hasAdditionalBrakingInformation rdfs:comment "Availability by the IM of additional information as defined in point (2) of point 4.2.2.6.2 of Regulation (EU) 2023/1693 - TSI OPE"@en .

:hasAutomaticDroppingDevice rdfs:comment "Automatic dropping device (ADD) fitted (to be indicated for each energy supply system the vehicle is equipped for)."@en .

:hasBallast rdfs:comment "Specifies whether track construction is with sleepers embedded in ballast or not."@en .

:hasBridge rdfs:comment "Whether or not a track is associated with a bridge."@en .

:hasCantDefficiencyCompensation rdfs:comment "Vehicle equipped with a cant deficiency compensation system (tilting vehicle)."@en .

:hasConnectingIM rdfs:comment "Indicates whether any neighbouring section of line belongs to different Infrastructure Manager"@en .

:hasCurrentLimitation rdfs:comment "Electric units equipped with power or current limitation function."@en .

:hasETCSRestrictionsConditions rdfs:comment "Indication whether restrictions or conditions due to partial compliance with the TSI CCS exist."@en .

:hasElectricShoreSupply rdfs:comment "Indication whether exists an installation of electric shore supply (fixed installation for servicing trains)."@en .

:hasEmergencyPlan rdfs:comment "Indication whether emergency plan exists."@en .

:hasEvacuationAndRescuePoints rdfs:comment "Indication of existence of evacuation and rescue points"@en .

:hasExternalCleaning rdfs:comment "Indication whether exists an installation of external cleaning facility (fixed installation for servicing trains) as defined in TSI INF"@en .

:hasHotAxleBoxDetector rdfs:comment "Existence of trackside HABD"@en .

:hasLevelCrossings rdfs:comment "Indication whether level crossings (including pedestrian track crossing) exist on the section of line."@en .

:hasLubricationDevicePrevention rdfs:comment "Possibility of preventing the use of the lubrication device (only if fitted with flange lubrication)."@en .

:hasNoiseLevelLimit rdfs:comment "Indicate, if there are any limits on noise levels."@en .

:maxNoiseLevelOfSoL rdfs:comment "Maximum allowed noise level in decibels (dB)."@en .

:hasOtherTrainProtection rdfs:comment "Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777. Indication if other train protection, control and warning systems in normal operation are installed lineside."@en .

:hasParkingBrake rdfs:comment "Indicates if a vehicle type (configuration) has a parking brake."@en,
    "Indicates whether all vehicles of this type are equipped with a parking brake."@en .

:hasPhaseSeparation rdfs:comment "Indication of existence of phase separation and required information."@en .

:hasPlatformCurvature rdfs:comment "Indication of the existence of the curvature of the platform."@en .

:hasRefuelling rdfs:comment "Indication whether exists an installation of refuelling (fixed installation for servicing trains) as defined in TSI INF."@en .

:hasRegenerativeBrake rdfs:comment "Indication whether regenerative braking is permitted or not."@en .

:hasSandRestocking rdfs:comment "Indication whether an installation of sand restocking exists (fixed installation for servicing trains)."@en .

:hasSandingPrevention rdfs:comment "Possibility of preventing the use of sanding."@en .

:hasSchematicOverviewOPDigitalForm rdfs:comment "The existence of a schematic overview of the operational point in digital form."@en .

:hasSevereWeatherConditions rdfs:comment "Climatic conditions on the line are severe according to European standard."@en .

:hasShuntingRestrictions rdfs:comment "Indicates the presence of shunting restrictions."@en .

:hasSystemSeparation rdfs:comment "Indication of existence of system separation"@en .

:hasTSITrainDetection rdfs:comment "Indication if there is any train detection system installed and fully compliant with the TSI CCS"@en .

:hasToiletDischarge rdfs:comment "Indication whether exists an installation of toilet discharge (fixed installation for servicing trains) as defined in TSI INF"@en .

:hasTrainIntegrityConfirmation rdfs:comment "Managing information about the completeness of the train"@en .

:hasWalkway rdfs:comment "Indication of existence of walkways"@en .

:hasWaterRestocking rdfs:comment "Indication whether exists an installation of water restocking (fixed installation for servicing trains) as defined in TSI INF"@en .

:hasWheelSlideProtectionSystem rdfs:comment "Indicates the presence of a wheel slide protection system."@en .

:highSpeedLoadModelCompliance rdfs:comment "For sections of line with a maximum permitted speed of 200 km/h or more. Information regarding the procedure to be used to perform the dynamic compatibility check."@en .

:hotAxleBoxDetectorGeneration rdfs:comment """Specific for the French Italian and Swedish networks. 
Generation of trackside hot axle box detector."""@en .

:hotAxleBoxDetectorIdentification rdfs:comment """Specific for the French, Italian and Swedish networks.
Applicable if trackside HABD is not TSI compliant, identification of trackside hot axle box detector."""@en .

:hotAxleBoxDetectorLocation rdfs:comment """Specific for the French Italian and Swedish networks.
Applicable if trackside HABD is not TSI compliant, localisation of trackside hot axle box detector."""@en .

:hotAxleBoxDetectorTSICompliant rdfs:comment """Specific for the French, Italian and Swedish networks.
Trackside HABD compliant to TSI means that the HABD Trackside is compliant with:
- EN 15437-1:2009 referred in TSIs (LOC&PAS: 4.2.3.3.2.2, WAG TSI: 4.2.3.4),
- Specific cases mentioned in TSIs (LOC&PAS TSI, WAG TSI)."""@en .

:idPhoneErtmsRadioBlockCenter rdfs:comment "Unique RBC identification (NID_C+NID_RBC) and calling number (NID_RADIO) as defined in the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]."@en .

:imCode rdfs:comment """Infrastructure manager means any body or firm responsible in particular for establishing, managing and maintaining railway infrastructure, including traffic management and control-command signalling; 
the functions of the infrastructure manager on a network or part of a network may be allocated to different bodies or firms. Definition in (Article 3(2))"""@en .

:organisationCode rdfs:comment """Four alpha-numeric code allocated by ERA to a body. It represents the Infrastructure Manager (IM) code in RINF.
Infrastructure manager means any body or firm responsible in particular for establishing, managing and maintaining railway infrastructure, including traffic management and control-command signalling; 
the functions of the infrastructure manager on a network or part of a network may be allocated to different bodies or firms. Definition in (Article 3(2))"""@en,
    "Infrastructure manager means any body or undertaking that is responsible in particular for establishing and maintaining railway infrastructure or a part thereof."@en .

:isOnOriginOfElementA rdfs:comment "Determines if the position of the topological element A in a relation is the origin of element A."@en .

:isOnOriginOfElementB rdfs:comment "Determines if the position of the topological element B in a relation is the origin of element B."@en .

:isQuietRoute rdfs:comment "Belonging to a 'quieter route' in accordance with Article 5b of TSI NOI."@en .

:kilometer rdfs:comment "Kilometer number of the kilometric post related to line identification defining the location of an infrastructure element."@en .

:kmPostName rdfs:comment "Name of the kilometric post (optional)."@en .

:length rdfs:comment "Generic super-property for different types of length"@en .

:lengthOfNetLinearElement rdfs:comment "Length of a topological linear element."@en .

:lengthOfPlatform rdfs:comment "The maximum continuous length (expressed in metres) of that part of platform in front of which a train is intended to remain stationary in normal operating conditions for passengers to board and alight from the train, making appropriate allowance for stopping tolerances."@en .

:lengthOfSectionOfLine rdfs:comment "Length between operational points at start and end of section of line."@en .

:lengthOfSiding rdfs:comment "Total length of the siding/stabling track expressed in metres where trains can be parked safely."@en .

:lengthOfTunnel rdfs:comment "Length of a tunnel in metres from entrance portal to exit portal."@en .

:letterMarking rdfs:comment "letter marking"@en .

:lineId rdfs:comment "Unique line identification or unique line number within Member State."@en .

:linearCoordinate rdfs:comment "Indicates the position of an object within a linear positioning system. For example, relative to a national railway line"@en .

:linesideDistanceIndicationFrequency rdfs:comment "Frequency of track lineside distance indications."@en .

:loadingGauge rdfs:comment "Maximum physical dimensions (height and width) to which an open rail wagon can be loaded"@en .

:loadingPlatformHeight rdfs:comment "Height of loading platform (for flat wagons and combined transport), given in mm."@en .

:localRulesOrRestrictions rdfs:comment "Existence of rules and restrictions of a strictly local nature"@en .

:mNvderun rdfs:comment "Entry of Driver ID permitted while running According to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]"@en .

:massPerWheel rdfs:comment "Mass per wheel, given in kg."@en .

:maxAxleLoadOfSoL rdfs:comment "Maximum permitted axle load, given in tons."@en .

:maxCurrentStandstillPantograph rdfs:comment "Indication of the maximum allowable train current at standstill expressed in amperes."@en .

:maxDistEndTrainFirstAxle rdfs:comment "Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777. Indication of maximum distance between end of train and first axle, given in millimetres, applicable for both sides (front and rear) of a vehicle or train."@en .

:maxFlangeHeight rdfs:comment "Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777. However, the parameter remains as it is also an ERATV parameter. Maximum flange height, given in millimetres."@en .

:maxImpedanceWheelset rdfs:comment """RINF: The value of maximum permitted impedance given in ohm in case of TSI non-compliance.
ERATV: Maximum impedance between opposite wheels of a wheelset."""@en .

:maxLengthVehicleNose rdfs:comment "Maximum length of the vehicle nose."@en .

:maxPermittedTrainLength rdfs:comment """Maximum train length in meters allowed on a section of line, without special permission, for the operation of freight trains. 
                            In accordance with Regulation (EU) 2024/1679, Article 15(2)(c), this maximum length must be supported by the infrastructure manager's ability 
                            to allocate sufficient train paths for freight trains of at least 740 meters (including the locomotive or locomotives), as required for the TEN-T network."""@en .

:maxTrainCurrent rdfs:comment "Indication of the maximum allowable train current expressed in amperes."@en .

:maxTunnelSpeed rdfs:comment "Indicate the speed limit in a tunnel"@en .

:maxbridgeWind rdfs:comment "Indicates the maximun wind speed for which the bridge can operate"@en .

:maximumAltitude rdfs:comment "Highest point of the section of line above sea level in reference to Normal Amsterdam's Peil (NAP)."@en .

:maximumAverageDeceleration rdfs:comment "Maximum train deceleration given in m/s²."@en .

:maximumBrakeThermalEnergyCapacity rdfs:comment "Maximum brake thermal energy capacity given in kJ"@en .

:maximumBrakingDistance rdfs:comment "The maximum value of the braking distance [in metres] of a train shall be given for the maximum line speed."@en .

:maximumContactWireHeight rdfs:comment "Indication of the maximum contact wire height expressed in metres."@en .

:maximumDesignSpeed rdfs:comment "Maximum design speed."@en .

:maximumInterferenceCurrentEvaluation rdfs:comment "Maximum interference current limits allowed for track circuits for a defined frequency band. "@en .

:maximumLocomotivesCoupled rdfs:comment "Maximum number of trainsets or locomotives coupled together in multiple operation."@en .

:maximumMagneticFieldDirectionX rdfs:comment "The maximum magnetic field limits allowed for axle counters (in dB µA/m) for a defined frequency band. Direction X."@en .

:maximumMagneticFieldDirectionY rdfs:comment "The maximum magnetic field limits allowed for axle counters (in dB µA/m) for a defined frequency band. Direction Y."@en .

:maximumMagneticFieldDirectionZ rdfs:comment "The maximum magnetic field limits allowed for axle counters (in dB µA/m) for a defined frequency band. Direction Z."@en .

:maximumPermittedMeterLoad rdfs:comment "Maximum permitted meter load, given in tons"@en .

:maximumPermittedSpeed rdfs:comment "Nominal maximum operational speed on the line as a result of infrastructure, energy and control, command signalling subsystem characteristics expressed in kilometres/hour."@en .

:maximumServiceBrake rdfs:comment "At maximum service brake: Stopping distance, Maximum deceleration, for the load condition 'design mass under normal payload' at the design maximum speed."@en .

:vehicleTypeMaximumCantDeficiency rdfs:comment "Part of the combination of maximum speed and maximum cant deficiency for which the vehicle was assessed. Corresponds to the maximum cant deficiency."@en .

:vehicleTypeMaximumSpeed rdfs:comment "Part of the combination of maximum speed and maximum cant deficiency for which the vehicle was assessed. Corresponds to the maximum speed."@en .

:maximumSpeedEmpty rdfs:comment "Maximum speed when empty"@en .

:maximumTrainDeceleration rdfs:comment "Limit for longitudinal track resistance given as a maximum allowed train deceleration and expressed in metres per square second."@en .

:maximumTrainLength rdfs:comment "Maximum train length allowed on a line or section"@en .

:measuredDistance rdfs:comment "Measured distance from the origin of the LRS."@en .

:meetsRequirementVehicleAuthorisation rdfs:comment "Type meets the requirements necessary for validity of the vehicle authorisation granted by one Member State in other MSs."@en .

:minAxleLoad rdfs:comment "Minimum (permitted) axle load, given in tonnes."@en .

:minRimWidth rdfs:comment "Minimum wheel rim width"@en .

:minimumConcaveVerticalRadius rdfs:comment "Minimum vertical concave curve radius capability."@en .

:minimumContactWireHeight rdfs:comment "Indication of the minimum contact wire height expressed in metres."@en .

:minimumConvexVerticalRadius rdfs:comment "Minimum vertical convex curve radius capability."@en .

:minimumHorizontalRadius rdfs:comment "Radius of the smallest horizontal curve of the track in metres."@en .

:minimumVerticalRadiusCrest rdfs:comment "Part of the minimum radius of vertical curve that indicates the crest"@en .

:minimumVerticalRadiusHollow rdfs:comment "Part of the minimum radius of vertical curve that indicates the hollow"@en .

:minimumWheelDiameter rdfs:comment "Maximum unguided length of fixed obtuse crossings is based on a minimum wheel diameter in service expressed in millimetres."@en .

:multipleTrainProtectionRequired rdfs:comment "Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777. Indication whether more than one train protection, control and warning system is required to be on-board and active simultaneously."@en .

:nationalLoadCapability rdfs:comment "National classification for load capability"@en .

:nationalRollingStockFireCategory rdfs:comment "Categorisation of how a passenger train with a fire on board will continue to operate for a defined time period - according to national rules if they exist."@en .

:nationalValuesBrakeModel rdfs:comment """Set of parameters for adapting the braking curves calculated by the ETCS on-board system to match accuracy, performance and safety margins imposed by the infrastructure manager.
It copies the content of Packet 3 or of Packet 203 as defined in the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]."""@en .

:nonCodedRestrictions rdfs:comment "Groups the non-coded restrictions, as a set of sentences. Can be used for any subClassOf `era:Restriction`."@en .

:numberElementsRakeFreightWagons rdfs:comment "Number of elements in the rake of freight wagons (only for subcategory 'rake of freight wagons')"@en .

:numberOfPantographsInContactWithOCL rdfs:comment "Number of pantographs in contact with the overhead contact line (OCL) (to be indicated for each energy supply system the vehicle is equipped for)."@en .

:oclType rdfs:comment "Type of OCL used for the test of current collection performance (to be indicated for each energy supply system the vehicle is equipped for) (only if number of raised pantographs is more than 1)."@en .

:offsetFromKilometricPost rdfs:comment "Relative distance from a reference kilometric post "@en .

:offsetFromOrigin rdfs:comment "Offset from the origin in a topological coordinate."@en .

:opName rdfs:comment "Name normally related to the town or village or to traffic control purpose."@en .

:opTypeGaugeChangeover rdfs:comment "Type of track gauge changeover facility."@en .

:parameterValue rdfs:comment "This property is used to link an applicability to the precise value of the parameter"@en .

:parkingBrakeMaximumGradient rdfs:comment "Maximum gradient on which the unit is kept immobilised by the parking brake alone (if the vehicle is fitted with it)."@en .

:passByNoiseLevel rdfs:comment "Pass-by noise level given in dB(A)."@en .

:passengerFlag rdfs:comment "Indicates whether a passenger train can perform commercial passenger activity at a primary location."@en .

:permissiblePayload rdfs:comment "Permissible payload for different line categories."@en .

:permissionChargingElectricEnergyTractionStandstill rdfs:comment "Point at which IM authorises charging of electric energy storage for traction purposes at standstill."@en .

:permitUseReflectivePlates rdfs:comment "Sections where is permitted to use the reflective plates on rail freight corridors, with a view to prioritise the current bottlenecks. Specific case for Belgium, France, Italy, Portugal and Spain until 1.1.2026"@en .

:permittedContactForce rdfs:comment "Indication of contact force allowed expressed in newton."@en .

:phaseInfoKm rdfs:comment "Part of the phase info of a track that indicates the location from the start of the line where the new value is valid."@en .

:phaseInfoLength rdfs:comment "Part of the phase info of a track that corresponds to the length of the phase separation in metres."@en .

:phaseInfoPantographLowered rdfs:comment "Part of the phase info of a track that shows whether a pantograph has to be lowered."@en .

:phaseInfoSwitchOffBreaker rdfs:comment "Part of the phase info of a track that shows whether the breaker has to be switched off."@en .

:phaseInfoChangeSupplySystem rdfs:comment "Part of the phase info of a track that corresponds to the single selection of Y=yes or N=no to show if the energy supply system changes"@en .

:phaseInfoDistanceType rdfs:comment "Part of the phase info of a track that corresponds to the single selection of 'MIN=minimum' or 'MAX=maximum' to show whether the length is a minimum distance between the inner contact strips of the pantographs or a maximum distance between the outer contact strips of the pantographs. Multiple strings for this parameter are accepted."@en .

:platformId rdfs:comment "Unique platform identification or unique platform number within an Operational Point."@en .

:portableBoardingAids rdfs:comment "Description of any portable boarding aids if considered in the design of the vehicle for meeting the PRM TSI requirements."@en .

:primaryLocationCode rdfs:comment "Primary location code developed for information exchange in accordance with the TSIs relating to the telematics applications subsystem."@en .

:publicNetworkRoaming rdfs:comment """Existence of roaming to a public network.
                         
                         In case of Y, provide the name of the public network(s) under parameter \"Details on GSM-R roaming to public networks\"."""@en .

:publicNetworkRoamingDetails rdfs:comment "If roaming to public networks is configured, please indicate to which networks, for which users and in which areas."@en .

:qNvsbtsmperm rdfs:comment "Permission to use service brake in target speed monitoring"@en .

:quasiStaticGuidingForce rdfs:comment "Quasi-static guiding force (if exceeds the limit defined in TSI or not defined in the TSI), given in kN."@en .

:radioNetworkId rdfs:comment "Unique identification of the GSM-R network the calling mobile station has to register with, as defined in the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]"@en .

:railSystemType rdfs:comment "(deprecated) Type of railway system. Can be \"High-speed\" or \"Conventional\". Deprecated due to the lack of information"@en .

:raisedPantographsDistance rdfs:comment "Part of the raised pantographs distance and speed of a track that corresponds to the minimum distance between pantographs, in metres."@en .

:raisedPantographsDistanceAndSpeed rdfs:comment "Indication of maximum number of raised pantographs per train allowed and minimum spacing centre line to centre line of adjacent pantograph heads, expressed in metres, at the given speed."@en .

:raisedPantographsNumber rdfs:comment "Part of the raised pantographs distance and speed of a track that corresponds to the number of pantographs."@en .

:raisedPantographsSpeed rdfs:comment "Indication of maximum number of raised pantographs per train allowed and minimum spacing centre line to centre line of adjacent pantograph heads, expressed in metres, at the given speed."@en .

:redLightsRequired rdfs:comment "Sections where permissive driving is possible in accordance with point 4.2.2.1.2 of TSI OPE"@en,
    "Sections where two steady red lights are required in accordance with TSI OPE"@en .

:relativeDistanceDangerPoint rdfs:comment "Distance in meters to the danger point"@en .

:relativePosition rdfs:comment "Indicates the position of an object relative to the linear coordinates of the associated topological object."@en .

:requiredSandingOverride rdfs:comment "Indication whether possibility to activate/deactivate sanding devices by driver, according to instructions from the Infrastructure Manager, is required or not. Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777."@en .

:schematicOverviewOP rdfs:comment "Document providing the schematic overview of the operational point"@en .

:shortestDistanceBetweenPantographsInContactWithOCL rdfs:comment "Shortest distance between two pantographs in contact with the OCL (to be indicated for each energy supply system the vehicle is equipped for; to be indicated for single and, if applicable, multiple operation) (only if number of raised pantographs is more than 1)."@en .

:sidingId rdfs:comment "Unique siding identification or number within an Operational Point."@en .

:specializedInfrastructure rdfs:comment "Special type of service on a line or a section of a line."@en .

:specificInformation rdfs:comment "Any relevant information from the IM relating to the line layout"@en .

:startOffsetFromOrigin rdfs:comment "Start offset of the section from the origin."@en .

:startingNoiseLevel rdfs:comment "starting noise level given in dB(A)."@en .

:staticAxleLoadExceptionalPayload rdfs:comment "Static axle load under exceptional payload."@en .

:staticAxleLoadNormalPayload rdfs:comment "Static axle load under normal payload."@en .

:staticAxleLoadWorkingOrder rdfs:comment "Static axle load in working order."@en .

:stationaryNoiseLevel rdfs:comment "stationary noise level given in dB(A)."@en .

:structuralCategory rdfs:comment "Structural category."@en .

:structureCheckLocation rdfs:comment "Localisation of structures requiring specific checks"@en .

:subsetName rdfs:comment "A subset of elements with common characteristics could be identified with a unique name/id."@en .

:subsidiaryLocationCode rdfs:comment "The numeric code for the subsidiary location"@en .

:subsidiaryLocationName rdfs:comment "The common name given to the subsidiary location"@en .

:switchRadioSystem rdfs:comment "Indication whether a switch over between different radio systems and no communication system whilst running exists."@en .

:systemSeparationInfoKm rdfs:comment """Part of the system separation info of a track. Indicates the location from the start of the line where the new value is valid.
The system separation info is the Indication of required several information on system separation."""@en;
  rdfs:label "System separation info Km"@en .

:systemSeparationInfoLength rdfs:comment """Part of the system separation info of a track that shows the length of the system separation in metres.
The system separation info is the Indication of required several information on system separation."""@en;
  rdfs:label "System separation info length"@en .

:systemSeparationInfoSwitchOffBreaker rdfs:comment """Part of the system separation info of a track that shows whether the breaker has to be switched off.
The system separation info is the Indication of required several information on system separation."""@en;
  rdfs:label "System separation info switch off breaker"@en .

:systemSeparationInfoChangeSupplySystem rdfs:comment """Part of the system separation info of a track that shows whether the supply system has to be changed.
The system separation info is the Indication of required several information on system separation."""@en;
  rdfs:label "System separation info change supply system"@en .

:systemSeparationInfoPantographLowered rdfs:comment """Part of the system separation info of a track that shows whether the pantograph has to be lowered.
The system separation info is the Indication of required several information on system separation."""@en;
  rdfs:label "System separation info  pantograph lowered"@en .

:tNvcontact rdfs:comment """Maximum time without a safe message from Radio Block Center before train reacts in seconds.
According to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]"""@en;
  rdfs:label "T_NVCONTACT"@en .

:tNvovtrp rdfs:comment """Maximum time for overriding the train trip in seconds.
According to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]"""@en;
  rdfs:label "T_NVOVTRP"@en .

:tenGISId rdfs:comment "Indication of the GIS identity (GIS ID) of the section of TEN-T database to which the track belongs"@en;
  rdfs:label "TEN geographic information system identity (GIS ID)"@en .

:thermalCapacityDistance rdfs:comment "Thermal capacity distance. If no reference case is indicated."@en;
  rdfs:label "Thermal capacity distance"@en .

:thermalCapacityGradient rdfs:comment "Thermal capacity gradient (If no reference case is indicated)"@en;
  rdfs:label "Thermal capacity gradient"@en .

:thermalCapacitySpeed rdfs:comment "Thermal capacity speed (If no reference case is indicated)"@en;
  rdfs:label "Thermal capacity speed"@en .

:thermalCapacityTime rdfs:comment "Thermal capacity time (If no reference case is indicated)"@en;
  rdfs:label "Thermal capacity time"@en .

:tiltingSupported rdfs:comment "Deprecated according to the amendment to the Regulation (EU) 2019/777. Indication whether tilting functions are supported by ETCS."@en;
  rdfs:label "Indication whether tilting functions are supported by ETCS"@en .

:totalVehicleMass rdfs:comment "Total vehicle mass (for each vehicle of the unit), given in kg."@en;
  rdfs:label "Total vehicle mass"@en .

:trackId rdfs:comment "Unique track identification or unique track number within operational point or section of line"@en;
  rdfs:label "Identification of track"@en .

:trainIntegrityOnBoardRequired rdfs:comment "Indication whether train confirmation from on-board is required to access the line for safety reasons."@en;
  rdfs:label "Train integrity confirmation from on-board (not from driver) necessary for line access"@en .

:tsiCompliant rdfs:comment "Indicates if a certain property is TSI compliant.The reason for deprecation is that it is used in SKOS \"OtherPantographHeads\" and \"TsiPantographHeads\" to indicate in the first case if a SKOS concept is not tsiCompliant (false) and in the second case that the concept is tsiCompliant (true). These two SKOS were originally one SKOS, \"PantographHeads\". Currently with the two SKOS the property is redundant."@en;
  rdfs:label "Tsi compliant"@en .

:tsiSwitchCrossing rdfs:comment "Switches and crossings are maintained to in service limit dimension as specified in TSI."@en;
  rdfs:label "TSI compliance of in-service values for switches and crossings"@en .

:tunnelIdentification rdfs:comment "Unique tunnel identification or unique tunnel number within Member State"@en;
  rdfs:label "Tunnel identification"@en .

:typeVersionNumber rdfs:comment "Serial number that identifies a vehicle type."@en;
  rdfs:label "Type version number"@en .

:umax2 rdfs:comment "Highest non-permanent voltage (Umax2) for France on lines not compliant with values defined in the EN50163:2004+A1:2007+A2:2020+A3:2022"@en;
  rdfs:label "Umax2 for the French network"@en .

:uopid rdfs:comment "Code composed of country code and alphanumeric operational point code."@en;
  rdfs:label "Unique OP ID"@en .

:usesGroup555 rdfs:comment "Indication if group 555 is used trackside or whether onboard has Voice SIM Card support for Group ID 555."@en;
  rdfs:label "GSM-R use of group 555"@en .

:vNvallowovtrp rdfs:comment """Speed limit allowing the driver to select the  override  function in km/h
According to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]"""@en;
  rdfs:label "V_NVALLOWOVTRP"@en .

:vNvsupovtrp rdfs:comment """Override speed limit to be supervised when the \"override\" function is active in km/h.
According to the specification referenced in Appendix A-1, index [C]"""@en;
  rdfs:label "V_NVSUPOVTRP"@en .

:vehicleContactForce rdfs:comment "Mean contact force."@en;
  rdfs:label "Mean contact force"@en .

:vehicleKinematicGaugeOther rdfs:comment "Vehicle kinematic gauge that corresponds to other gauges assessed using the kinematic method"@en;
  rdfs:label "Vehicle kinematic gauge other"@en .

:vehicleMaxSandingOutput rdfs:comment "Vehicle Maximum sanding output, given in grams per second."@en;
  rdfs:label "Vehicle max sanding output"@en .

:vehicleNumber rdfs:comment "European Vehicle Number. Numeric identification code as defined in Appendix 6 of Annex II of the EVR Regulation."@en;
  rdfs:label "European Vehicle Number"@en .

:vehiclePantographHead rdfs:comment "Pantograph head geometry (to be indicated for each energy supply system the vehicle is equipped for)."@en;
  rdfs:label "Vehicle pantograph head"@en .

:vehiclesComposingFixedFormation rdfs:comment "Number of vehicles composing the fixed formation (for fixed formation only). Note: the value is mandatory for all vehicle categories. If the vehicle is composed of only one car, the indicated value shall be '1'."@en;
  rdfs:label "Vehicles composing fixed formation"@en .

:verificationCCS rdfs:comment "Unique number for EC declarations in accordance with Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2019/250."@en;
  rdfs:label "EC declaration of verification for track relating to compliance with the requirements from TSIs applicable to control, command signalling subsystem"@en .

:verificationENE rdfs:comment "Unique number for EC declarations in accordance with Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2019/250."@en;
  rdfs:label "EC declaration of verification for track relating to compliance with the requirements from TSIs applicable to energy subsystem"@en .

:verificationINF rdfs:comment "Unique number for EC declarations in accordance with Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2019/250."@en;
  rdfs:label "EC declaration of verification for infrastructure element relating to compliance with the requirements from TSIs applicable to infrastructure subsystem"@en .

:verificationSRT rdfs:comment "Unique number for EC declarations in accordance with Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2019/250."@en;
  rdfs:label "EC declaration of verification relating to compliance with the requirements from TSIs applicable to railway tunnel"@en .

:voiceOperationalCommImpl rdfs:comment "Voice and operational communication implementation."@en;
  rdfs:label "Voice operational communication implementation"@en .

:wheelSetGaugeTransformationMethod rdfs:comment "Wheel gauge transformation method. Defined if more than one wheel gauges have been selected."@en;
  rdfs:label "Wheel set gauge transformation method"@en .

<http://www.w3.org/ns/org#identifier> rdfs:comment "Código o identificador, como por ejemplo el CIF de una empresa, que permite identificar de forma inequívoca a una organización. Existen muchos códigos de identificación tanto nacionales como internacionales. Esta ontología no obliga al uso de ningún esquema en concreto. Los códigos de identificación utilizados en cada caso se deberían indicar mediante el uso de la propiedad “datatype” del valor del identificador. El uso de la propiedad “datatype” para especificar el esquema de notación utilizado está en consonancia con las buenas prácticas recomendadas para el uso de la propiedad `skos:notation`, de la que esta propiedad es una especialización."@es,
    "Donne un identifiant, comme par exemple le numéro d'enregistrement d'une entreprise, qui peut être utilisé comme identifiant unique pour l'Organisation. De nombreux schémas nationaux et internationaux sont disponibles. Cette ontologie reste neutre par rapport au schéma utilisé. Le schéma particulier utilisé devrait être indiqué par le `datatype` de la valeur de l'identifiant. Utiliser les datatypes pour distinguer les schémas de notation est cohérent avec les bonnes pratiques pour `skos:notation` dont cette propriété est une spécialisation."@fr,
    "Gives an identifier, such as a company registration number, that can be used to used to uniquely identify the organization. Many different national and international identier schemes are available. The org ontology is neutral to which schemes are used. The particular identifier scheme should be indicated by the datatype of the identifier value.  Using datatypes to distinguish the notation scheme used is consistent with recommended best practice for `skos:notation` of which this property is a specialization."@en,
    "Indica un identificatore univoco per l'organizzazione, come ad esempio la partita IVA di un'azienda. Molti schemi di identificazione a livello nazionale e internazionale sono disponibili allo scopo. L'ontologia ORG è neutrale rispetto allo schema da utilizzare. Lo schema di identificazione dovrebbe essere indicato dal datatype del valore dell'identificatore. L'uso del datatype per distinguere lo schema di identificazione è coerente con le best practice per `skos:notation`, di cui questa proprietà è una specializzazione."@it,
    "組織を一意に識別するために使用できる会社登録番号などの識別子を与えます。"@ja;
  rdfs:label "identifiant"@fr, "identificatore"@it, "identifier"@en, "tiene identificador"@es .

:LevelCrossing rdfs:comment "A level crossing is an intersection where a railway line crosses a road or a path at the same level. It can be used for the implementation of the ETCS trackside or to identify potential collision scenarios"@en;
  rdfs:label "Level crossing"@en .

:Switch rdfs:comment "A unit of track comprising two fixed rails (stock rails) and two movable rails (switch rails) used to direct vehicles from one track to another track."@en;
  rdfs:label "Switch"@en .

:changeActivity rdfs:comment "Links an ERA resource (e.g. Body) to an activity representing a change affecting that resource."@en;
  rdfs:label "change activity"@en .

:Activity rdfs:comment "ERA-specific activity aligned with prov:Activity (W3C PROV-O), used to describe changes affecting ERA resources."@en;
  rdfs:label "Activity"@en .

:alternativeCode rdfs:comment "Alternative code resulting of the integration of RISC into SRMO for managing organisation code"@en;
  rdfs:label "Alternative Code"@en .

:revokedCode rdfs:comment "Organisation code value that was revoked."@en;
  rdfs:label "revoked code"@en .

:ERTMSErrorChangeRequest rdfs:comment "SKOS concept representing a change request (CR) classified as an error in the ERTMS specifications and analysed by the Agency to identify whether it may prevent the system from providing normal service under Article 10 of the CCS TSI."@en;
  rdfs:label "ERTMS error change request"@en .

:changeRequestPreventsService rdfs:comment "Indicates whether the given ERTMS error change request may prevent the system from providing normal service if not implemented or applied."@en;
  rdfs:label "change request prevents service"@en .

:onboardRecordingDevice rdfs:comment "Onboard equipment - recording device"@en;
  rdfs:label "Onboard equipment - recording device"@en .

:otherCCSRadioSystemOnboard rdfs:comment "Other CCS radio systems onboard"@en;
  rdfs:label "Other CCS radio systems onboard"@en .

:otherCCSSystemOnboard rdfs:comment "Other CCS systems onboard"@en;
  rdfs:label "Other CCS systems onboard"@en .

:AxleSpacing rdfs:comment "Stub class for axle spacing "@en;
  rdfs:label "Axle spacing"@en .

:axleSpacingDistanceA rdfs:comment "Position of the axles along the unit: a: Distance between axles"@en;
  rdfs:label "Axle spacing, distance a"@en .

:axleSpacingDistanceB rdfs:comment "Position of the axles along the unit: b: Distance from end axle to the end of the nearest coupling plane"@en;
  rdfs:label "Axle spacing, distance b"@en .

:axleSpacingDistanceC rdfs:comment "Position of the axles along the unit: c: distance between two inside axles."@en;
  rdfs:label "Axle spacing, distance c"@en .

:axleSpacingExplanation rdfs:comment "Explanation of the values for a, b and c"@en;
  rdfs:label "Axle spacing, explanation for a, b, c"@en .

:BrakingPerformance rdfs:comment "Stub class for braking performance expressed as (lambda) brake weight/braked mass percentage, or braked mass"@en;
  rdfs:label "Braking performance"@en .

:withBrakedMass rdfs:comment "Braked mass."@en;
  rdfs:label "Braked mass"@en .

:withBrakedMassPercentage rdfs:comment "Braked mass percentage (lambda)."@en;
  rdfs:label "Braked mass percentage"@en .

:serviceBrakingProfile rdfs:comment "Service Brake: Stopping distance and deceleration profile for specific load condition at design maximum speed."@en;
  rdfs:label "maximum service braking"@en .

:BrakingProfile rdfs:comment "Stub class for braking profile under applicable load condition, stopping distance, deceleration and initial speed"@en;
  rdfs:label "Braking profile"@en .

:profileLoadConditionMass rdfs:comment "Load Condition mass defining the braking profile, at design maximum speed."@en;
  rdfs:label "profile defining load condition"@en .

:profileDeceleration rdfs:comment "Maximum train deceleration given in m/s² for a certain braking profile, at design maximum speed."@en;
  rdfs:label "max deceleration for braking profile at max speed"@en .

:profileStoppingDistance rdfs:comment "Maximum train stopping distance given in m for a certain braking profile, at design maximum speed."@en;
  rdfs:label "max train stopping distance for braking profile at max speed"@en .

:Restriction rdfs:comment "A restriction, condition of use, having its origin in a railway verification/certification/permission process."@en;
  rdfs:label "Restriction"@en .

:isConditionBasedRestriction rdfs:comment "The values to be mentioned are the ones defined in the issued vehicle type authorisation and/or vehicle authorisation for placing on the market."@en;
  rdfs:label "Condition based restriction of use"@en .

:isTimeBasedRestriction rdfs:comment "Some issued authorisation can include time-limited conditions for use. Time limitation is not a data provided by the applicant but a consequence of an authorisation decision (see Art 46(6) or regulation 2018/545)"@en;
  rdfs:label "Time based restriction of use"@en .

:VehicleRegistrationRestriction rdfs:comment "An `era:Restriction` which originates from a compliance check during the Vehicle's Registration."@en;
  rdfs:label "Vehicle Registration Restriction"@en .

:hasCompositeBrakeBlockRetrofitted rdfs:comment "Indicates if a vehicle's composite brake block is retrofitted"@en;
  rdfs:label "Composite brake block retrofitted"@en .

:VehicleTypeAuthorisationRestriction rdfs:comment """Restrictions, like coded and non-coded conditions for use, to be taken into account in the context of a Vehicle (Type) Authorisation.

The restrictions are recorded by the Authorising Entities, possibly deduced during underlying verification and certification processes by competent bodies, and if possible are documented with a link
to the legal reference and sections therein.

In most cases, the Restriction will be dependent of a VehicleTypeConfiguration."""@en;
  rdfs:label "Vehicle Type Authorisation Restriction"@en .

:VehicleTypeAuthorisationApplication rdfs:comment """The request, as submitted by the Applicant in line with (EU)2018/545, to allow the vehicle type authorisation and/or the vehicle authorisation for placing on the market.
The application consists of one or more authorisation cases as described in Art. 14 of (EU)2018/545, and for authorisations before the Fourth Railway Package, a HistoricalAuthorisationCase must be used.

The outcome of the application process is a `era:VehicleAuthorisation` or `era:VehicleTypeAuthorisation`."""@en;
  rdfs:label "Vehicle Type Authorisation Case"@en .

:isPreEngagementApplication rdfs:comment "Determines if the Application for Vehicle (Type) Authorisation is determining a preEngagementBaseline, and not yet the authorisation itself."@en;
  rdfs:label "is pre-engagement application"@en .

:preEngagementBaseline rdfs:comment "Denotes the opinion on the approach proposed by the applicant in the pre-engagement application, including a determination of the version of the TSIs and national rules that are to be applied for the subsequent application for authorisation"@en;
  rdfs:label "Pre-engagement baseline"@en .

:VehicleTypeAuthorisationCase rdfs:comment """The process, as selected by the Applicant in line with (EU)2018/545, allowing the vehicle type authorisation and/or the vehicle authorisation for placing on the market.
The type of authorisation cases are described in Art. 14 of (EU)2018/545, and for authorisations before the Fourth Railway Package, a HistoricalAuthorisationCase must be used.

Each authorisation case supports a VehicleTypeAuthorisationApplication and is determined by exactly one VehicleType, and a set of Vehicles, which can be empty in some cases.

For authorisations before the (EU)2018/545 legislation, use `era:VehicleAuthorisationCase."""@en;
  rdfs:label "Vehicle Type Authorisation Case"@en .

:VehicleAuthorisationCase rdfs:comment """The process allowing the vehicle authorisation for placing in service (APIS).

This authorisation case supported a Vehicle Application for APIS and was determined by exactly one set of Vehicles and if available a VehicleType.

For the Authorisation as per EU 2018/545, use era:VehicleTypeAuthorisationCase, which covers all authorisations types under that legislation."""@en;
  rdfs:label "Vehicle APIS Case"@en .

:areaOfUse rdfs:comment "(32) ‘area of use of a vehicle’ means a network or networks within a Member State or a group of Member States in which a vehicle is intended to be used;"@en;
  rdfs:label "Area of Use"@en .

:authorisingMemberState rdfs:comment "Indicates the member state where a vehicle type has been authorized. Not to be confused with Area Of Use."@en;
  rdfs:label "Member State of authorisation"@en .

:safetyDeclaration rdfs:comment "Reference to the written declaration by the proposer referred to in Article 3(11) of Regulation (EU) No 402/2013"@en;
  rdfs:label "CSM-REA Safety Declaration"@en .

:configDependentCompliance rdfs:comment "This property is used to link a vehicle type with its conformity checks, through the authorisation case(s)"@en;
  rdfs:label "configuration dependent conformities/compliances"@en .

:VehicleTypeAuthorisationCheck rdfs:comment """A verification result as executed by a competent body on a section of a legal reference. The check can be positive or negative, and in the latter case, a restriction is expected.

This Class is used to improve the link between verification outcomes and the verified scope of that process, and support its structured documentation."""@en;
  rdfs:label "Vehicle Type Authorisation Compliance Check"@en .

:configDependentCondition rdfs:comment "This property is used to link a vehicle type with its restrictions, through the authorisation case(s)"@en;
  rdfs:label "configuration dependent conditions of use and other restrictions"@en .

:typeRegistrationMethod rdfs:comment "The registration method which was used in the vehicle type authorisation process."@en;
  rdfs:label "Type registration method"@en .

:hasStrictLocalHistoricalTouristUse rdfs:comment "Strictly local, historical or tourist use"@en;
  rdfs:label "Strictly local, historical or tourist use"@en .

:quieterRoutesNoiseCategory rdfs:comment "The quieter routes apply only to wagons in the scope of the Wagon TSI (refer to Article 5a of the Noise TSI)."@en;
  rdfs:label "Quieter route exempted country"@en .

:VehicleTypeAuthorisation rdfs:comment """(16) the decision issued by the authorising entity based on reasonable assurance that the applicant and the entities involved in the design,
manufacture, verification and validation of the vehicle type have fulfilled their obligations and responsibilities in order to ensure conformity with the essential
requirements of the applicable legislation enabling that a vehicle manufactured according to this design may be placed on the market and may be used safely in the
area of use of the vehicle type according to the conditions for use of the vehicle and other restrictions, when applicable, specified in the vehicle type authorisation
and to be applied to all vehicle authorised in conformity to this type;"""@en;
  rdfs:label "Vehicle Type Authorisation"@en .

:vehicleTypeAuthorisationHolder rdfs:comment "Indicates the vehicle type authorisation holder."@en;
  rdfs:label "Vehicle type authorisation holder"@en .

:VehicleTypeConfigParameterSet rdfs:comment "Stub class linking a VehicleTypeConfiguration (`era:forConfiguration`) with parameters of the VehicleType that depend on that configuration."@en;
  rdfs:label "Vehicle type configuration parameter set"@en .

:axleSpacingDistance rdfs:comment "Position of the axles along the unit. a: Distance between axles; b: Distance from end axle to the end of the nearest coupling plane; c: distance between two inside axles."@en;
  rdfs:label "Axle spacing"@en .

:hasOnboardEnergyMeasurement rdfs:comment "TSI conform energy meter for billing purposes installed on board."@en;
  rdfs:label "Energy meter installed"@en .

:forConfiguration rdfs:comment "The configuration for which the ParameterSet or Restriction is valid."@en;
  rdfs:label "for Configuration"@en .

:VehicleTypeConfiguration rdfs:comment "The combination of supported Gauge, Energy Systems and/or CCO Systems for a vehicle type"@en;
  rdfs:label "Vehicle type configuration"@en .

:hasBrakingPerformance rdfs:comment "Braking performance of a vehicle type (configuration)."@en;
  rdfs:label "Has braking performance"@en .

:hasOCLChargeableTractionStorage rdfs:comment "Vehicle equipped with electric energy storage for traction purposes and with the function of charging with OCL at standstill."@en;
  rdfs:label "Has OCL-chargeable onboard storage system for traction"@en .

:hasVehicleTypeConfiguration rdfs:comment "It is used to link a vehicle type configuration set with a vehicle type configuration"@en;
  rdfs:label "has vehicle type configuration"@en .

:emergencyBrakeProfile rdfs:comment "Emergency Brake: Stopping distance and deceleration profile for each load condition per design maximum speed."@en;
  rdfs:label "Emergency braking"@en .

:etcsBaselineIncompleteCompatibility rdfs:comment "If the version is not fully compatible it shall be indicated in brackets."@en;
  rdfs:label "ETCS baseline incompatibility indication"@en .

:forOnBoardClassA rdfs:comment "Configuration corresponding to the rinf concept in ETC CCS."@en;
  rdfs:label "for onboard class A"@en .

:forOnBoardClassB rdfs:comment "Configuration corresponding to the rinf concept in \"Other Protection Control and Warnings concepts."@en .

:forWheelSetGauge rdfs:comment "Configuration corresponding to the rinf concept in wheel set gauge concepts"@en .

:forEnergySupplySystem rdfs:comment "Configuration corresponding to the rinf concept in energy supply system."@en .

:forLineCategory rdfs:comment "Allows to link a configuration parameter set to a line category"@en .

:alternativeTypeName rdfs:comment """Alternative name of a vehicle type.
For the type name, use `rdfs:label`."""@en .

:atoOnBoardImplementation rdfs:comment "ATO on-board implementation."@en .

:configDependentParameter rdfs:comment "This property is used to link a vehicle type with a configuration parameter set, which is a group of parameters which depend on a VehicleTypeConfiguration."@en .

:hasEddyCurrentBrakePrevention rdfs:comment "Possibility of preventing the use of the eddy current track brake (only if fitted with eddy current brake)"@en .

:hasEddyCurrentBrake rdfs:comment "Eddy current track brake fitted. New property defined to distinguish it from eddyCurrentBraking which is a RINF SKOS property."@en .

:etcsOnboardSystemVersions rdfs:comment "Envelope of legally operated ETCS system versions"@en .

:hasFerromagneticWheelMaterial rdfs:comment "Wheel material is ferromagnetic."@en .

:hasCantDeficiencyCompensation rdfs:comment "Vehicle equipped with a cant deficiency compensation system (tilting vehicle)."@en .

:hasOnboardDerailmentFunction rdfs:comment "Presence of derailment prevention and detection function."@en .

:hasSignalProcessingDerailmentFunction rdfs:comment "Presence of derailment prevention and detection by signal processing."@en .

:includedVersionsVariant rdfs:comment """Reserved for VehicleTypes authorised under the Fourth Railway Package (Since 2018/545).

Complementing the vehicleTypeNumber of 10 characters, is a combination of maximally two 3-digit groups ('ZZZ[-VVV]'), which represent
the type's evolution after creation, as versions (of variants), variants (of variants), be it never as variants of versions."""@en .

:hasMagneticBrakePrevention rdfs:comment "Possibility of preventing the use of the magnetic track brake (only if fitted with magnetic brake)"@en .

:hasMagneticBrake rdfs:comment "Magnetic track brake fitted. New property defined to distinguish it from magneticBraking which is a RINF SKOS property."@en .

:maxDistConsecutiveAxle rdfs:comment "Indication of maximum permitted distance between two consecutive axles in case of TSI non-compliance, given in millimetres."@en .

:numberOfToilet rdfs:comment "Number of toilets."@en .

:operationalMassNormalPayload rdfs:comment "Operational mass under normal payload."@en .

:operationalMassWorkingOrder rdfs:comment "Operational mass in working order."@en .

:hasMandatoryParkingBrake rdfs:comment "All vehicles of this type must be equipped with a parking brake (parking brake mandatory for vehicles of this type)."@en .

:permissiblePayloadForLineCategory rdfs:comment "Permissible payload for different line categories."@en .

:hasRegenerativeBrakePrevention rdfs:comment "Possibility of preventing the use of the regenerative brake (only if fitted with regenerative brake)."@en .

:prioritySeat rdfs:comment "Number of priority seats (min to max number)."@en .

:prmAccessibleToilet rdfs:comment "Number of PRM accessible toilets."@en .

:radioSwitchOverSpecialCondition rdfs:comment "Special conditions implemented on-board to switch over between different radio systems. Given as combination of systems installed on board ('System XX'_'System YY')."@en .

:isPassByNoiseMeasuredUnderReferenceConditions rdfs:comment "Pass-by noise level was measured under reference conditions."@en .

:sleepingPlace rdfs:comment "Number of sleeping places (min to max number)"@en .

:isTransportableOnFerry rdfs:comment "Indicates the suitability for transport on ferries."@en .

:vehicleTypeManufacturer rdfs:comment "VehicleType Manufacturer identification and contact data"@en .

:vehicleTypeNumber rdfs:comment """Each type of vehicle shall receive a number consisting of 10 digits with the structure as in Annex III of the ERATV Decision.

For the full Vehicle Identifier, use `dcterms:identifier`.
For the complement before Fourth Railway package, use `era:includedVersions`.
For the complements after the Fourth Railway Package, use `era:includedVersionsVariant`."""@en .

:vehicleTypeSubCategory rdfs:comment "Indicates the further classification (but not any family/platform) of vehicles within a vehicle category."@en .

:wagonDerailmentFunction rdfs:comment "Presence and type of derailment detection and prevention function(s)."@en .

:wheelchairSleepingPlace rdfs:comment "Number of wheelchair accessible sleeping places (min to max number)."@en .

:wheelchairSpace rdfs:comment "Number of wheelchair spaces (min to max number)."@en .

:compatibleWithLineCategory rdfs:comment "Indicates the EN line categories with which a vehicle type is compatible."@en .

:trainControlSwitchOverSpecialCondition rdfs:comment "Special conditions implemented on-board to switch over between different train protection control and warning systems. Given as combination of systems installed on board ('System XX'_'System YY')."@en .

:etcsBaselineCompatibility rdfs:comment "If the ETCS Baseline.Version is not fully compatible, it shall be indicated (use era:etcsBaselineIncompleteCompatibility for textual)."@en .

:assessedCantDeficiency rdfs:comment "Cant deficiency (maximum uncompensated lateral acceleration) for which the vehicle has been assessed. For dual gauge vehicles values for each gauge have to be indicated."@en .

:vehicleContactForceFormula rdfs:comment "Contact force formula."@en .

:vehicleTypePlatform rdfs:comment "The Type Holder's name for the Type's Family/Platform, as encoded in the first set of 3 numbers in the `dcterms:identifier` of the Type."@en .

:legacyRadioSystemComment rdfs:comment "ADDITIONAL COMMENTS ON: Class B or other radio systems installed"@en .

:protectionLegacySystemComment rdfs:comment "ADDITIONAL COMMENTS ON: Class B or other train protection, control and warning systems installed"@en .

:hasFlangeLubrication rdfs:comment "Indicates if the vehicle type is fitted for flange lubrication."@en .

:ECDeclaration rdfs:comment "EC Declaration of Verification/Conformity/Suitability for Use, as issued by an Applicant in the process of certification/verification activities for IC's or subsystems."@en .

:lengthOfNonStoppingArea rdfs:comment "Length of a Non-stopping area."@en .

:wasInvalidatedBy rdfs:comment "Annotation property used to express that a property is no more valid for a given legal regime."@en .

:includedVersions rdfs:comment """Reserved for VehicleTypes authorised before the Fourth Railway Package.

Complementing the vehicleTypeNumber of 10 characters, is maximally one 3-digit group ('XXX'), which represent
the type's evolution after creation."""@en .

vpa:EvidenceDocument rdfs:comment "Issued by an AppropriateBody, it is the summary of its formal and accredited verification process, enabling the receiver (RequestingBody) to issue a Request for a Permission to the PermittingBody."@en .

:Compliance rdfs:comment "A Compliance result, having its origin in a railway verification/certification/assessment process."@en .

vpa:Compliance rdfs:comment "Regroups the result of a compliance check on a specific section of an applicable Requirement as registered in Documented Evicence. If needed, links this examined section to a specific Restriction."@en .

:DocumentSet rdfs:comment "A collection of documents belonging together, as they contain - as a set - evidence in an ERA process like registration or authorisation."@en .

vpa:Restriction rdfs:comment "Issued by an Appropriate Body in connection with its documented evidence on a certain requirement, it contains all aspects to take into account in order to accept the DocumentedEvidence as proof, enabling the scope of the Permission. It is possible that the Restriction limits the Permission in the same way."@en .

:VehicleAuthorisation rdfs:comment """(15) the decision issued by the authorising entity based on a reasonable assurance that the applicant and the entities involved in the design,
manufacture, verification and validation of the vehicle have fulfilled their respective obligations and responsibilities in order to ensure conformity with essential
requirements of the applicable legislation or to ensure conformity with the authorised type enabling that the vehicle may be placed on the market and may be used safely in the
area of use according to the conditions for use and other restrictions, when applicable, specified in the vehicle authorisation and in the vehicle type authorisation;"""@en .

vpa:Permission rdfs:comment "Issued by a PermittingBody, it enables - mostly because of legal frameworks in place - the RequestingBody to execute the processes covered under these requirement frameworks."@en .

vpa:Case rdfs:comment "A clearly separated part of a Request, identified clearly by its Scope(s). Each Case has an individual PermissionType as objective. A Request consists out of minimally one Case."@en .

:VehicleAuthorisationNotification rdfs:comment """The notification, as submitted by the Applicant in line with (EU)2018/545, informs the authorising entity of the vehicle(s set) to be updated according to Article 16.
The notification consists of one case as described in Art. 16 of (EU)2018/545, containing the vehicle type and EVNs, and linking to the required Evidence.

The outcome of the notification process is an added comment in the  `era:VehicleAuthorisation`, if accepted by the Authorising Entity."""@en .

vpa:Request rdfs:comment "Issued by a Requesting Body to a PermittingBody, and supported by at least one Case, while being supported by the necessary DocumentedEvidence, it intends to enable the reception of a Permission."@en .

vpa:Scope rdfs:comment "A collection of Scopes together defining a Case. Scope is mostly the specific material object of the Case, where the Case groups them together."@en .

:nationalPropertyMandatory rdfs:comment "Declares whether a national registration property concept is mandatory for the member state context where it applies. This property is asserted on SKOS Concepts in the NationalRegistrationProperties concept scheme and is used by SHACL constraints to verify presence of required national properties."@en .

:nationalPropertyMaxLength rdfs:comment "Declares the maximum allowed string length for a national registration property concept. This property is asserted on SKOS Concepts in the NationalRegistrationProperties concept scheme and is used by SHACL constraints to validate string literal lengths for era:nationalPropertyValue."@en .

:nationalPropertyExpectedDatatype rdfs:comment "The URI of the expected XSD datatype for the value of a national registration property (e.g. http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string, http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer). This property is asserted on SKOS Concepts in the NationalRegistrationProperties concept scheme, and is used by SHACL SPARQL constraints to dynamically validate the datatype of era:nationalPropertyValue."@en .

:manufacturingSerialNumber rdfs:comment "Manufacturing serial number as marked on the vehicle frame."@en .

:registeredManufacturingSerialNumber rdfs:comment "The manufacturing serial or series number as stated during the Registration. May differ from the `era:manufacturingSerialNumber` of the Vehicle itself."@en .

:relatedCertificate rdfs:comment "Identification number of a related Certificate."@en .

:CertificationLevelDocument rdfs:comment "Certification Level Document, as issued by a NoBo in the process of its certification/verification activities [RFU-STR-001]. The class can be reused as well for DeBo and AsBo certificates."@en .

:additionalOtherVehicleConditions rdfs:comment "Identification of other applicable bilateral or multilateral agreements other than RIV, RIC, TEN, TEN-CW, TEN-GE, …."@en .

:vehicleDependentCondition rdfs:comment "Conditions for use of the vehicle and other restrictions on how the vehicle may be used"@en .

:VehicleRegistrationCase rdfs:comment """Vehicle Registrations can be created and modified using a specific Registration Case as listed in `3.2.2.   Registration cases` of the EVR Decision.

Each registration case will have as its scope:
- a set of vehicles of which the registration needs creating/updating.
- if present, the authorisation delivered for these vehicles and/or vehicle type to which they belong."""@en .

:coversHighSpeed rdfs:comment "Covers for `type of operation` of passenger transport services at speeds higher than 250km/h, or speeds considered as such through TEN-T."@en .

:CABAssessmentCheck rdfs:comment "A compliance check as executed by a Conformity Assessment Body. The class can be used NoBo, DeBo and/or AsBo checks."@en .

:CABAuditCheck rdfs:comment "A compliance observation as executed by a Conformity Assessment Body in an audit. The class can be used NoBo, DeBo and/or AsBo checks."@en .

:UnlimitedValidityConstraint rdfs:comment "A validity constraint signalling that the CLD has no expiry — no end date or duration should be specified."@en .

:ValidityConstraint rdfs:comment "Abstract superclass for constraints on CLD validity periods, as prescribed by a TSI or Decision 2010/713/EU."@en .

:CABAddition rdfs:comment "An additionally allowed Option, Added Function which was confirmed by a CAB"@en .

:VehicleRegistration rdfs:comment """Vehicle Registration serves to ensure traceability of vehicles and their history: vehicles should be registered under a European vehicle number in a vehicle register. Each
member state designated a registration entity responsible for the registering of vehicles and the processing and update of information in relation to vehicles that entity has registered in the European Vehicle Register.

A vehicle registration groups the information for a (set of) vehicle(s) as in Appendix 4 of Commission Implementing Decision (EU) 2018/1614 of 25 October 2018."""@en .

:inVehicleSeries rdfs:comment "Manufacturing series of a vehicle."@en .

:resultReport rdfs:comment "Report about the assessment/audit result (either NoBo File or NoBo Conformity Assessment Report, with identifier, revision, date)"@en .

:VehicleRegistrationApplication rdfs:comment """Keepers should fill in an application for registration with the required information (Appendix 4 of EVR Decision).  A keeper shall submit an application for registration through
the European Vehicle Register to a Member State of its choice within the area of use of the vehicle.

A VehicleRegistrationApplication traces the state of this process, links to the RegistrationCase(s), and a registration entity independent of any railway undertaking which
will be responsible for the processing of the applications and updating of data in the European Vehicle Register."""@en .

:registeringMemberState rdfs:comment "Indicates the member state where a vehicle type has been registered. Not to be confused with Area Of Use of the registration (deduced from the authorisation)."@en .

:usedInEradis rdfs:comment "Indicates whether a parameter or property is used in ERADIS register/domain."@en .

:TechnicalSpecForInteroperability rdfs:comment "Technical Specification for Interoperability"@en .

:isOTIFMember rdfs:comment "Property to identify in VKM register if the era:Body or org:Organization is from OTIF"@en .

:VehicleKeeperMarking rdfs:comment "The class used to relate a Vehicle Keeper Marking (VKM) properties for the purpose of the VKM register."@en .

:ForbiddenAssessmentConstraint rdfs:comment "A validity constraint signalling that the combination of CLD type and assessment module is structurally not permitted under this TSI."@en .

:validityStatement rdfs:comment "Statement about the validity of the CLD"@en .

:borderPointStation rdfs:comment "Link a certificate to the border station for operations"@en .

:evrIndex rdfs:comment "Index code used in the original definition of a parameter in EVR Annex 2 - Table 1."@en .

:registrationCaseType rdfs:comment "Type of registration case according to Annex 2 - 3.2.2 Registration Cases (e.g., new registration, modification, change of ECM)."@en .

:verificationRSTWAG rdfs:comment "Unique number for EC declarations in accordance with Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2019/250."@en .

:transportationVolumePassenger rdfs:comment "The transportation volume for passenger services."@en .

:manufacturingYear rdfs:comment "Indicates the year in which a vehicle is manufactured."@en .

:transportationVolumeFreight rdfs:comment "The transportation volume for freight services."@en .

:NationalRegistrationProperty rdfs:comment "A property defined at national level by a member state for vehicle registration purposes. Each member state may define its own set of such properties, identified by a national property identifier string. This class avoids creating individual era: predicates for each member-state-specific registration field. The member state is determined by the registeringMemberState of the parent VehicleRegistrationCase."@en .

:VehicleRegistrationCheck rdfs:comment """A verification result as executed by a competent body on a section of a legal reference. The check can be optional, positive or negative, and in the latter case, a restriction is expected.

This Class is used to improve the link between verification outcomes and the verified scope of that process, and support its structured documentation.

It must be used in the context of the Vehicle Registration process."""@en .

:registeredManufacturingYear rdfs:comment "The manufacturing year as stated during the Registration. May differ from the `era:manufacturingYear` of the Vehicle itself."@en .

:vehicleOwner rdfs:comment "Indicates the organization that owns a vehicle or wagon."@en .

:additionalVehicleConditions rdfs:comment "Identification of applicable bilateral or multilateral agreements such as RIV, RIC, TEN, TEN-CW, TEN-GE, …. Other conditions can be added elsewhere."@en .

:areaOfOperation rdfs:comment "(33) ‘area of operation’ means a network or networks within one or more Member States where a railway undertaking intends to operate.;"@en .

:nationalPropertyIdentifier rdfs:comment "Identifies the national registration property by pointing to a SKOS Concept from the NationalRegistrationProperties concept scheme. Each concept carries the field name, expected datatype, and is grouped in a skos:Collection per member state."@en .

:cldValidityRule rdfs:comment "Links a legal resource (typically a consolidated version of a TSI) to a validity constraint governing a specific CLD type + module combination."@en .

:registeredCodedConditions rdfs:comment "The coded conditions as stated during the Registration."@en .

:isOptional rdfs:comment "Indicates whether a compliance check concerns an optional function or optional requirement."@en .

:resultStatement rdfs:comment "Statement about the assessment/audit result"@en .

:VehicleSet rdfs:comment "A set of vehicles together forming the Scope of a registration/authorisation case or involved as on whole in another process."@en .

:CABRestriction rdfs:comment "A Restriction which was issued by a CAB"@en .

:vkmCode rdfs:comment "VKM code is an alphanumeric5 code, consisting of 2 to 5 letters."@en .

:sequenceStatement rdfs:comment "Statement about the superceded CLD"@en .

:coversDangerousGoods rdfs:comment "Covers for a `type of operation` involving the freight transport of dangerous goods"@en .

:VehicleSeries rdfs:comment "Collection of Vehicles belonging together, for instance in the scope of an Authorisation or Registration Case."@en .

:vkmNational rdfs:comment "VKM code is an alphanumeric5 code, consisting of 2 to 5 letters."@en .

:nationalPropertyValue rdfs:comment "The actual value of this national registration property. The datatype of the literal should match the expected datatype declared via era:nationalPropertyExpectedDatatype."@en .

:coversOnlyShunting rdfs:comment "Covers for a `type of operation` limited to only shunting operations"@en .

:hasNationalRegistrationProperty rdfs:comment "Links a vehicle registration case to a national-level registration property defined by a member state. Each member state may define its own set of such properties, identified by a national property identifier string. This avoids creating individual era: predicates for each member-state-specific registration field."@en .

:resultAnnex rdfs:comment "Annex of the assessment/audit result"@en .

:vehicleKeeperMarking rdfs:comment "Indicates the Vehicle Keeper Marking (VKM) associated with a vehicle."@en .

:CABEvidence rdfs:comment "A `era:DocumentSet` which mainly contains Certification Level Documents or Certificates of Conformity from a Conformity Assessment Body."@en .

:organisationSize rdfs:comment "The size of a given organisation or body."@en .

:vehicleECM rdfs:comment "Indicates the organization that is charge of maintenance."@en .

:faxNumber rdfs:comment "Fax number of a body."@en .

:MaxDurationConstraint rdfs:comment "A validity constraint that imposes an upper bound on the CLD validity period. Being a subclass of time:DurationDescription, it uses time:years (and potentially time:months, time:days) to express the maximum allowed duration."@en .

:CABCertificate rdfs:comment "A `vpa:EvidenceDocument` from a Conformity Assessment Body examining any other reference than a TSI or its annexes."@en .

:complianceResult rdfs:comment "The outcome of a compliance check, expressed as a SKOS concept."@en .

:minInServiceWheelDiameter rdfs:comment "Minimum in-service wheel diameter expressed in millimetres."@en .

