:atoCommunicationSystem :tsiOPEAppendixD2Index "3.4.9";
  dcterms:relation :atoGradeAutomation, :etcsBaseline, :atoSystemVersion, :etcsDataCommApp;
  skos:scopeNote """ATO system communication system to the specification referenced in TSI CCS (4.2.4 & 4.2.19).
                           Parameter only applicable when ETCS Baseline > 4 MR1 and ATO is implemented"""@en .

:atoGradeAutomation :tsiOPEAppendixD2Index "3.4.8";
  dcterms:relation :etcsBaseline;
  skos:scopeNote """ATO is an optional function added in ETCS B4, only available under L2. See: TSI CCS, 4.2.4 & 4.2.19.

                       Parameter only applicable when ETCS Baseline > 4 MR1 and ATO is implemented

                       ATO Grad of Automation is defined in TSI CCS/Appendix A/Index 084/Reference SUBSET-125/ERTMS/ATO System Requirement Specification v. 1.0.0/chapter 5.1.1.4"""@en .

:etcsBaseline :tsiOPEAppendixD2Index "3.2.7";
  dcterms:relation :etcsLevelType;
  skos:scopeNote "The ETCS baseline needs to be provided for each available ETCS Level. See: TSI CCS (Table A2)"@en .

:atoSystemVersion :tsiOPEAppendixD2Index "3.4.8";
  dcterms:relation :atoGradeAutomation, :etcsBaseline;
  skos:scopeNote """ATO is an optional function added in ETCS B4, only available under L2. See: TSI CCS, 4.2.4 & 4.2.19.

                     Parameter only applicable when ETCS Baseline > 4 MR1 and ATO is implemented"""@en .

:etcsLevelType :tsiOPEAppendixD2Index "3.2.7";
  dcterms:relation :etcsBaseline, :cantDeficiencyBasicSSP, :etcsDegradedSituation, :etcsMVersion,
    :etcsSystemCompatibility, :etcsTransmittedTrackConditions, :gsmRActiveMobiles, :rbcID,
    :rbcPhone;
  skos:scopeNote """The different ERTMS / ETCS application levels are a way to express the possible operating relationships between track and train. 
  
Level definitions are principally related to the track side equipment used, to the way the track side information reaches the on-board units and to which functions are processed in the track side and in the on-board equipment respectively.

If ETCS is on the trackside (one or more levels are selected), all other ETCS parameters (from 1.1.1.3.2.2 to 1.1.1.3.2.10) are applicable and mandatory to be populated with values .
If the line is only equipped with Class B, this should be reflected in Parameter 1.1.1.3.5.3, and this parameter is “N”(not applicable). 

The ETCS value NTC is only relevant when the line is dual equipped with ETCS (i.e., balises are placed in the track) and Class B system, and both systems are in operation at the same time. 
In those cases, this parameter should be filled relevant ETCS Level and repeated with the value NTC.
  
If the line is only equipped with Class B, this should be reflected in Parameter 1.1.1.3.5.3, and this parameter etcsLevelType should not be used. 

See: TSI CCS (Subset-026, Chapter 2, 2.6)"""@en .

:conditionalRegenerativeBrake :tsiOPEAppendixD2Index "3.3.7";
  :usedInRCCCalculations true;
  dcterms:relation :contactLineSystemType;
  skos:scopeNote """When regenerative braking is \"allowed under conditions\", a document must be provided under 1.1.1.2.2.4.1.

For RINF XML data sets:
As long as the data provision through XML data sets is allowed, an XML attribute called “Set” will be used to link the value of this parameter to the parameter 1.1.1.2.2.1.1 / ECS_SystemType"""@en .

:conditionsAppliedRegenerativeBraking :tsiOPEAppendixD2Index "3.3.7";
  dcterms:relation :contactLineSystemType;
  skos:scopeNote """The value of this parameter should be either a reference to a file name or an external link to a document. 
If a file name is provided, the Infrastructure Manager (IM) must upload a document with the same file name using the \"Reference Documents Management\" functionality in the RINF application. The document must be in electronic format and available in two official EU languages. In this case, the parameter value must be repeated for each document. 
If an external link is provided, the IM must ensure that the document is available at the provided link."""@en .

:conditionsSwitchClassBSystems :tsiOPEAppendixD2Index "3.4.3";
  dcterms:relation :ETCS, :switchProtectControlWarning;
  skos:scopeNote """The details of the conditions to switch between Class B train protection systems must be published.

The value of this parameter should be either a reference to a file name or an external link to a document. 
If a file name is provided, the Infrastructure Manager (IM) must upload a document with the same file name using the \"Reference Documents Management\" functionality in the RINF application. The document must be in electronic format and available in two official EU languages. In this case, the parameter value must be repeated for each document. 
If an external link is provided, the IM must ensure that the document is available at the provided link."""@en .

:switchProtectControlWarning :tsiOPEAppendixD2Index "3.4.2";
  dcterms:relation :conditionsSwitchTrainProtectionSystems;
  skos:scopeNote "Switch over between different systems whilst running. Installation depends on local conditions. "@en .

:eddyCurrentBraking :tsiOPEAppendixD2Index "3.4.5";
  :usedInRCCCalculations true;
  skos:editorialNote "This property has been modified to be a RINF parameter (its eratvIndex is deleted). It is treated as a SKOS by RINF and as a boolean by ERATV. A new ERATV datatype property has been defined, eddyCurrentBrakingFitted with boolean values."@en;
  skos:scopeNote """The use of both brakes is allowed or not under exterior conditions (depending on the features of the train engines for example).
The RINF can't be filled without more precisions."""@en .

