    <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2021-05-18> .

:axleSpacingExplanation skos:scopeNote "The parameter should currently be considered independent of a Vehicle Configuration.";
  dcterms:isRequiredBy <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2023-09-08>, <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2019-06-16>,
    <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2021-05-18> .

:profileLoadConditionMass skos:scopeNote """The mass, defined by the load condition, as under
- era:designMassExceptionalPayload
- era:designMassNormalPayload
- era:designMassWorkingOrder.
"""@en;
  dcterms:isRequiredBy <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2023-09-08>, <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2019-06-16>,
    <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2021-05-18> .

:isConditionBasedRestriction skos:scopeNote "The details of any specified condition is to be specified within a non-coded restriction (e.g. concerned constituents where CV modules apply)."@en;
  skos:note "Harmonised restriction code 4.2"@en;
  :evrIndex "11.9.1" .

:areaOfUse skos:scopeNote "Not applicable for Authorisation Cases of `vpa:permissionType era-va-authcase:PRE4RP`."@en;
  dcterms:isRequiredBy <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2023-09-08>, <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2019-06-16>,
    <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2021-05-18>;
  :evrIndex "3.1" .

:axleSpacingDistance skos:scopeNote "The parameter should currently be considered independent of a Vehicle Configuration.";
  dcterms:isRequiredBy <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2023-09-08>, <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2019-06-16>,
    <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2021-05-18> .

:hasOnboardEnergyMeasurement skos:scopeNote """The parameter must have as range a VehicleTypeConfigParameterSet, of which the VehicleTypeConfiguration
at least contains one EnergySystem, from the ones recorded under `era:energySupplySystem`. Further, all of the ENE supply systems mentioned under that parameter
must have a value for this parameter `era:energyMeterInstalled`."""@en .

:hasOCLChargeableTractionStorage skos:scopeNote """The parameter must have as range a VehicleTypeConfigParameterSet, of which the VehicleTypeConfiguration
at least contains one EnergySystem, from the ones recorded under `era:energySupplySystem`. Further, all of the ENE supply systems mentioned under that parameter
must have a value for this parameter `era:hasOCLChargeableTractionStorage`."""@en;
  dcterms:isRequiredBy <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2023-09-08> .

:etcsOnboardSystemVersions skos:scopeNote "See: TSI CCS (Subset-026, Chapter 7, 7.5.1.79 M_VERSION, and 7.5.1.9.)"@en;
  dcterms:isRequiredBy <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2023-09-08> .

:hasOnboardDerailmentFunction skos:scopeNote "Only applicable for Traction Locomotives, which are intended to detect derailments or precursors to derailments in freight wagons hauled by the locomotive, with equipment fulfilling this function shall be located entirely on board the locomotive."@en;
  dcterms:isRequiredBy <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2023-09-08> .

:hasSignalProcessingDerailmentFunction skos:scopeNote "Only applicable for Traction Locomotives, intended to process signals emitted by freight wagons, if provided with Derailment Prevention Function (‘DPF’) or Derailment Detection Function (‘DDF’) as defined in point 4.2.3.5.3 of TSI WAG."@en;
  dcterms:isRequiredBy <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2023-09-08> .

:minDistConsecutiveAxle skos:scopeNote "Indication of minimum permitted distance between two consecutive axles, given in millimetres."@en;
  dcterms:isRequiredBy <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/oj> .

:permissiblePayloadForLineCategory skos:scopeNote "The parameter should currently be considered independent of a Vehicle Configuration." .

:wagonDerailmentFunction skos:scopeNote "The parameter is only applicable for VehicleTypes with the FreightWagon category."@en;
  dcterms:isRequiredBy <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/2023-09-08> .

:compatibleWithLineCategory skos:scopeNote "The EN line categories upon which the type can operate."@en .

:etcsBaselineCompatibility skos:scopeNote ""@en .

:assessedCantDeficiency skos:scopeNote "For dual gauge vehicles, values for each gauge shall be indicated.";
  dcterms:isRequiredBy <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665/oj>;
  :wasInvalidatedBy <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg_impl/2019/776/oj/eng> .

:vehicleContactForceFormula skos:scopeNote """The formula of the function shall represent the curve describing the value of the contact force in relation to the speed.
Static and maximum forces are given only for the maximum permitted line speed (see parameter number 1.1.1.1.2.5)."""@en .

:ECDeclaration skos:scopeNote """Every EC Declaration is the outcome of a process assisted by a recognised/accredited body (`vpa:AppropriateBody`) which is allowed to issue the supporting
CLD's to the `vpa:RequestingBody` needing it for a specific purpose, as defined in the IOD or SD.
EC Declarations MUST refer to the required CLDs using `dcterms:requires` which can be grouped as `vpa:Evidence` in authorisation/registration processes."""@en .

:CertificationLevelDocument skos:scopeNote """Every CLD is the result of a process by a recognised/accredited body (`vpa:AppropriateBody`) which is allowed to issue it to a `vpa:RequestingBody` needing it for a specific purpose,
as defined in the IOD or SD. Several CLDs can support EC Declarations."""@en;
  owl:disjointWith :ECDeclaration;
  :usedInEradis true .

:CABAssessmentCheck skos:scopeNote """This class is used to model the compliance details, typically of a era:CertificationLevelDocument (through `vpa:checkedCompliance`):
- [Scope of /Exemptions from Assessment], using the property `era:complianceResult` and a reference to the TSI or Section which was in scope or exempted;
- Assessment result can be documented using standard ontology properties."""@en;
  owl:disjointWith :CABAuditCheck;
  :usedInEradis true .

:CABAuditCheck skos:scopeNote """This class is used to model the audit observations of a era:CertificationLevelDocument (through `vpa:checkedCompliance`):
- [Scope of /Exemptions from Audit], using the property `era:complianceResult` and a reference to the TSI or Section which was in scope or exempted;
- Audit result can be documented using standard ontology properties."""@en;
  :usedInEradis true .

:CABAddition skos:scopeNote """This class is used to express the inverse of a typical Restriction, namely the approval of an Option or Added Function.

This information is stored under the `era:CertificationLevelDocument`'s `era:CABAssessmentCheck` like shown in the example."""@en;
  :usedInEradis true .

:resultReport skos:scopeNote """See RFU-STR-001, A.2
- 13.Reference to accompanying EC Assessment Report [R5,R14,R22,R27,R31,R32]
- 14.Reference to accompanying NoBo File [R3.c,R5,R6,R7,R13,R14,R15,R18,R19,R35]"""@en;
  :usedInEradis true .

:validityStatement skos:scopeNote "See RFU-STR-001, A.2 - 15.Validity of the Certification: any timeframes/conditions of validity shall be stated.[R3.b,R11,R36]"@en .

:previousVehicleNumber skos:scopeNote "This must be 8 or 12 numerical digits"@en;
  :evrIndex "1.2" .

:verificationRSTWAG skos:scopeNote ""@en;
  :evrIndex "6.2" .

:areaOfOperation skos:scopeNote "The SKOS Concept Scheme should contain al networks existing in the EU."@en;
  :usedInEradis true .

:resultStatement skos:scopeNote "See RFU-STR-001, A.2 - 10.Statement about the Assessment Results"@en;
  :usedInEradis true .

:CABRestriction skos:scopeNote """This class is used to express a Restriction, as formulated by a CAB.

This information is stored under the `era:CertificationLevelDocument`'s `era:CABAssessmentCheck` like shown in the example."""@en;
  :usedInEradis true .

:sequenceStatement skos:scopeNote "See RFU-STR-001, A.2 - 16.(Where applicable) Reference to superseded CLD in case of restricted or amended EC Certificate. [R37]"@en;
  :usedInEradis true .

:resultAnnex skos:scopeNote "See RFU-STR-001, A.2 - 12.(Where used) Reference to Annex of CLD [R5, R14]"@en;
  :usedInEradis true .

:CABCertificate skos:scopeNote """In order to distinguish between `EC Certificates` (which are a subset of `era:CertificationLevelDocument`) and more general `Certificates of Conformity`
as delivered for any other conformity check towards annexes of Directives, also outside of the railway system."""@en .

:complianceResult skos:scopeNote "Links a compliance check to a SKOS concept representing the compliance result, such as fully compliant, partially compliant or a qualified not compliant result."@en .

:minInServiceWheelDiameter skos:scopeNote """The minimum TSI value is 330 mm and this shall be used as a default value unless advised otherwise. If the value of the wheel diameter is bigger than 330 mm, it has to be specified.
New lines are assumed to be compliant with the TSI INF. When the line is compliant to TSI the default value of 330 mm has to be presented."""@en .

